//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// XAUUSD Adaptive Master STRATEGY — P5 Strategy Tester counterpart
// =============================================================================
// STRATEGY/INDICATOR PARITY: this file is a byte-for-byte duplicate of the
// canonical pine/XAUUSD_Adaptive_Master.pine decision logic (everything
// from the version constants through the P5 recorder/statistics), with
// exactly two differences: (1) this declaration line (indicator() ->
// strategy()), and (2) a "STRATEGY EXECUTION" block appended at the very
// end that places real strategy.entry()/strategy.exit() orders using the
// SAME finalTradeApproved/candIsLong/signalSl/signalTp2 values the
// indicator already computes — never a second, independently-derived
// trading algorithm. Parity is enforced by an exact-text-diff test
// (tests/pine_p5_strategy_parity.test.js), not by a shared library import
// (Pine has no local multi-file import mechanism without publishing a
// library to TradingView's cloud, which is out of scope for this phase).
// Do NOT hand-edit this file's decision logic independently of the
// indicator — regenerate it from the indicator source instead.
// =============================================================================
// This is the canonical Pine source for the XAUUSD Adaptive Master indicator.
// Do not fork a second competing script — extend this one in later phases.
//
// P1 gave regime + correction. P2 gave confirmed market structure (pivots,
// HH/HL/LH/LL, BOS/CHoCH, sweeps, PDH/PDL, displacement, anchored range).
// P3 is the FIRST phase authorized to reach BUY/SELL — it adds the five
// approved entry models (TC/PB/BO/MR/SR), a regime×model×direction
// eligibility matrix, setup/trigger/confirmation states, an entry-location
// (do-not-chase) gate, logical SL→targets→RR construction (in that order,
// never reverse-engineered), a 0-100 quality score, and a freeze-once
// signal state machine. See the "DECISION ENGINE (P3)" section below for
// the full pipeline and docs/PINE_P3.md for the complete specification.
//
// THE PERMANENT INVARIANT (unchanged in spirit since P1, now finally load-
// bearing): WAIT is the default and the common case. `contractAction` is
// computed as `finalTradeApproved ? (side) : "WAIT"` — `finalTradeApproved`
// is the conjunction of EVERY gate in the pipeline; if even one is false,
// the result is always "WAIT". Trend alone, a bare BOS, a bare CHoCH, a
// bare sweep, an active correction, a late/overextended entry, RR below
// minimum, or quality below threshold can never by themselves produce a
// trade — see the "FINAL PROOF" table in docs/PINE_P3.md and the review
// report for the exhaustive list of what was verified.
// =============================================================================

strategy("XAUUSD Adaptive Master Strategy", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 20, max_labels_count = 20, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = true, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0)

// ── Version constants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CONTRACT_VERSION = 1
INDICATOR_VERSION = "0.4.0"

// ── Inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
debugMode = input.bool(false, "Debug Mode (show internal state table + regime tint)", group = "Debug")

// Regime engine
persistenceBars      = input.int(3, "Regime Persistence (confirmed bars before an official regime change)", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
emaFastLen           = input.int(20, "EMA Fast Length", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
emaSlowLen           = input.int(50, "EMA Slow Length", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
emaSlopeLookback     = input.int(5, "EMA Slow Slope Lookback (bars)", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
adxDiLen             = input.int(14, "DI Length", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
adxSmoothing         = input.int(14, "ADX Smoothing", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
adxTrendThreshold    = input.float(20.0, "ADX Trend Threshold", minval = 0.0, group = "Regime")
atrLen               = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
atrAvgLen            = input.int(100, "ATR% Rolling Average Length", minval = 10, group = "Regime")
highVolMultiplier    = input.float(1.5, "High-Volatility ATR-Ratio Threshold", minval = 1.0, group = "Regime")
bbLen                = input.int(20, "Bollinger Length (Compression Measure)", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
bbMult               = input.float(2.0, "Bollinger Mult", minval = 0.5, group = "Regime")
bbWidthAvgLen        = input.int(100, "BB-Width Rolling Average Length", minval = 10, group = "Regime")
compressionRatioMax  = input.float(0.6, "Compression: BB-Width Ratio Threshold (<=)", minval = 0.05, group = "Regime")
diBalanceThreshold   = input.float(6.0, "Range: |DI+ - DI-| Balance Threshold (<=)", minval = 0.0, group = "Regime")
transitionLookback   = input.int(5, "Transition Lookback (bars since EMA cross / trend loss)", minval = 1, group = "Regime")
flipLookback         = input.int(10, "Chop: Direction-Flip Lookback (bars)", minval = 4, group = "Regime")
flipCountThreshold   = input.int(4, "Chop: Direction-Flip Count Threshold", minval = 1, group = "Regime")

// Higher-timeframe context (foundation only — not used to gate anything in P1/P2)
// NOTE: "60" is a fixed placeholder default, not an approved 5m/15m/30m→HTF
// mapping. That mapping is an architecture decision for a later phase; this
// input exists so an operator/later phase can override it per execution
// timeframe without editing code.
htfTimeframe = input.timeframe("60", "Higher-Timeframe Context (placeholder default — override per execution TF)", group = "HTF")

// Correction engine
swingLookback        = input.int(20, "Correction: Swing High/Low Lookback (prior confirmed bars)", minval = 3, group = "Correction")
corrAtrMultiplier    = input.float(1.2, "Correction: Displacement ATR Multiplier", minval = 0.1, group = "Correction")
corrMomentumLookback = input.int(3, "Correction: Momentum (EMA-fast) Lookback Bars", minval = 1, group = "Correction")
corrResolveConfirmBars = input.int(2, "Correction: Resolution Confirm Bars", minval = 1, group = "Correction")

// Session (deterministic UTC hour boundaries — a documented placeholder
// baseline, not a claim of exact interbank session accuracy)
asiaStartUtc   = input.int(0, "Asia Session Start (UTC hour)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Session")
londonStartUtc = input.int(8, "London Session Start (UTC hour)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Session")
nyStartUtc     = input.int(13, "New York Session Start (UTC hour)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Session")
otherStartUtc  = input.int(21, "Other/Off-Session Start (UTC hour)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Session")

// Structure engine (new in P2)
pivotLeftBars        = input.int(5, "Pivot Left Bars", minval = 1, group = "Structure")
pivotRightBars       = input.int(5, "Pivot Right Bars (confirmation lag)", minval = 1, group = "Structure")
swingEqAtrMult       = input.float(0.1, "Swing Equality Tolerance (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, group = "Structure")
displacementAtrMult  = input.float(1.5, "Displacement: Min Body Size (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, group = "Structure")
displacementBodyRatioMin = input.float(0.6, "Displacement: Min Body/Range Ratio", minval = 0.1, maxval = 1.0, group = "Structure")
displacementCloseLocMin  = input.float(0.7, "Displacement: Min/Max Close-Location Within Candle", minval = 0.5, maxval = 1.0, group = "Structure")
rangeAnchorPersistBars = input.int(5, "Anchored Range: Persistence Bars Required to Anchor", minval = 2, group = "Structure")
maxActiveLevels      = input.int(3, "Structure: Max Retained Active Levels Per Side", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = "Structure")

// Decision engine (P3) — setup/trigger recency windows, per model
tcSetupLookback   = input.int(10, "TC: Displacement Recency Lookback (bars)", minval = 1, group = "P3 Models")
pbSetupLookback   = input.int(10, "PB: Correction-Resolution Recency Lookback (bars)", minval = 1, group = "P3 Models")
boRetestAtrTol    = input.float(0.3, "BO: Retest ATR Tolerance", minval = 0.05, group = "P3 Models")
boRetestMaxBars   = input.int(15, "BO: Max Bars to Wait for Retest", minval = 1, group = "P3 Models")
mrBoundaryAtrTol  = input.float(0.5, "MR: Range-Boundary Overshoot ATR Tolerance", minval = 0.05, group = "P3 Models")
mrDisplacementBlockBars = input.int(2, "MR: Opposing-Displacement Block Recency (bars)", minval = 0, group = "P3 Models")

// Decision engine (P3) — entry-location / do-not-chase. Overextension is
// price-distance-based (ATR-normalized). Lateness is CHRONOLOGICAL —
// bars elapsed since each model's own setup-origin event — and is
// deliberately a SEPARATE, TIGHTER threshold than that model's own
// setup-recency window (tcSetupLookback/pbSetupLookback/boRetestMaxBars
// above), so a trigger can be technically still-eligible per its setup
// window yet independently flagged ENTRY_LATE for being stale relative to
// this stricter bound (see the P3 review's §2 fix). MR and SR have no
// entry here — their triggers are same-bar by construction (see
// candSetupOriginBar below) and are therefore provably never late.
overextendAtrMult  = input.float(2.5, "Entry Location: Overextension ATR Multiple", minval = 0.5, group = "P3 Entry")
tcMaxEntryLateBars = input.int(5, "TC: Max Bars From Displacement to Trigger", minval = 1, group = "P3 Entry")
pbMaxEntryLateBars = input.int(5, "PB: Max Bars From Resolution to Trigger", minval = 1, group = "P3 Entry")
boMaxEntryLateBars = input.int(10, "BO: Max Bars From Breakout to Reclaim", minval = 1, group = "P3 Entry")

// Decision engine (P3) — SL/TP construction
slAtrBuffer        = input.float(0.25, "SL: ATR Buffer Beyond Structure", minval = 0.0, group = "P3 Risk")
slAtrFallback      = input.float(1.5, "SL: ATR Fallback Distance (no structural anchor found)", minval = 0.5, group = "P3 Risk")
tp1RMultiple       = input.float(1.0, "TP1: R-Multiple", minval = 0.1, group = "P3 Risk")
tp2RMultipleDefault = input.float(2.0, "TP2: Default R-Multiple (no structural objective found)", minval = 0.5, group = "P3 Risk")
tp2RMultipleCap    = input.float(3.0, "TP2: Max R-Multiple Cap", minval = 1.0, group = "P3 Risk")
minRR              = input.float(1.5, "Minimum RR", minval = 0.1, group = "P3 Risk")

// Decision engine (P3) — quality gate
qualityThreshold = input.float(65, "Quality Threshold (0-100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "P3 Quality")

// Decision engine (P3) — manual news suppression (Pine cannot know live news;
// this is a manual, user-controlled toggle only — never automatic).
newsSuppressed = input.bool(false, "News Suppression Active (manual)", group = "P3 Safety")

// ── Confirmed-bar discipline ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every PERSISTENT state transition in this script (regime, structure,
// correction) is gated behind `confirmedBar`. Candidates/raw measurements
// may be computed every bar (for debug visibility of "what would happen if
// this bar closed"), but nothing persistent commits until the bar is
// confirmed — this is what makes every *official*/tracked field
// non-repainting.
confirmedBar = barstate.isconfirmed

// ── Core measurements (each one documented — no indicator stacking) ──────
emaFast = ta.ema(close, emaFastLen)
emaSlow = ta.ema(close, emaSlowLen)
// Slow-EMA slope over N bars — smoother/more reliable trend-direction
// confirmation than a single-bar EMA delta.
emaSlope = emaSlow - emaSlow[emaSlopeLookback]

[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(adxDiLen, adxSmoothing)

atrVal = ta.atr(atrLen)
atrPct = close != 0 ? atrVal / close * 100.0 : 0.0
atrPctAvg = ta.sma(atrPct, atrAvgLen)
atrRatio = atrPctAvg > 0 ? atrPct / atrPctAvg : 1.0

[bbBasis, bbUpper, bbLower] = ta.bb(close, bbLen, bbMult)
bbWidth = bbBasis != 0 ? (bbUpper - bbLower) / bbBasis : 0.0
bbWidthAvg = ta.sma(bbWidth, bbWidthAvgLen)
bbWidthRatio = bbWidthAvg > 0 ? bbWidth / bbWidthAvg : 1.0

// ── Higher-timeframe context (foundation only) ────────────────────────────
// Non-repaint pattern: the `[1]` INSIDE the request.security() expression
// asks for the value as of the PREVIOUS, already-closed HTF bar — never the
// currently-forming one — regardless of how far into the current HTF bar the
// chart's own execution-timeframe clock currently is. Combined with
// `lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off` (never lookahead_on), this guarantees
// the HTF value used here was fully knowable at the time it is read; it is
// never a "future" HTF bar leaking backward onto earlier execution-TF bars.
// HTF information becomes knowable exactly at the close of each HTF bar —
// not before, and (via the `[1]` shift) never mid-formation.
htfEmaFastExpr() => ta.ema(close, emaFastLen)
htfEmaSlowExpr() => ta.ema(close, emaSlowLen)
htfEmaFast = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTimeframe, htfEmaFastExpr()[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
htfEmaSlow = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTimeframe, htfEmaSlowExpr()[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
htfBias = htfEmaFast > htfEmaSlow ? "BULL" : (htfEmaFast < htfEmaSlow ? "BEAR" : "FLAT")

// ── Regime candidate (raw, recomputed every bar; NOT the official regime) ─
strongTrend = adxVal >= adxTrendThreshold
trendUp     = emaFast > emaSlow and emaSlope > 0
trendDown   = emaFast < emaSlow and emaSlope < 0
highVol     = atrRatio >= highVolMultiplier
compressed  = (adxVal < adxTrendThreshold) and (bbWidthRatio <= compressionRatioMax)
diBalanced  = math.abs(diPlus - diMinus) <= diBalanceThreshold

barsSinceCross     = ta.barssince(ta.cross(emaFast, emaSlow))
barsSinceCrossSafe = na(barsSinceCross) ? transitionLookback + 1 : barsSinceCross
recentCross        = barsSinceCrossSafe <= transitionLookback

// "Trend strength lost recently" — was strong within the lookback, isn't now.
strongTrendPrior      = strongTrend[1]
barsSinceStrongTrend  = ta.barssince(strongTrend)
recentTrendLoss       = (not strongTrend) and strongTrendPrior and not na(barsSinceStrongTrend) and barsSinceStrongTrend <= transitionLookback

transitionCond = recentCross or recentTrendLoss

// Direction-flip count over a short lookback — evidence for CHOP_UNCERTAIN.
// Deliberately a small, fixed-size loop (bounded by flipLookback, a small
// input) — not a performance concern, and fully deterministic.
int flipCount = 0
for i = 1 to flipLookback - 1
    dirNow  = close[i] - close[i + 1] > 0 ? 1 : (close[i] - close[i + 1] < 0 ? -1 : 0)
    dirPrev = close[i + 1] - close[i + 2] > 0 ? 1 : (close[i + 1] - close[i + 2] < 0 ? -1 : 0)
    if dirNow != dirPrev and dirNow != 0 and dirPrev != 0
        flipCount += 1
choppy = flipCount >= flipCountThreshold

// Deterministic priority chain — first match wins, so branches never overlap
// ambiguously. Each rule's evidence is named above and documented inline.
regimeCandidate = highVol ? "HIGH_VOLATILITY" :
     compressed ? "COMPRESSION" :
     (trendUp and strongTrend) ? "BULL_TREND" :
     (trendDown and strongTrend) ? "BEAR_TREND" :
     transitionCond ? "TRANSITION" :
     (diBalanced and not choppy) ? "RANGE" :
     "CHOP_UNCERTAIN"

// ── Regime persistence / hysteresis (confirmed-bar gated) ─────────────────
// A candidate must hold for `persistenceBars` CONSECUTIVE CONFIRMED bars
// before it becomes the official regime — this is the deterministic
// anti-flicker mechanism. Defaults to CHOP_UNCERTAIN (the most conservative
// state) until enough history accumulates, rather than an undefined value.
var string officialRegime   = "CHOP_UNCERTAIN"
var string lastCandidate    = "CHOP_UNCERTAIN"
var int    regimeStreak     = 0
var string priorOfficialRegime = "CHOP_UNCERTAIN"

if confirmedBar
    priorOfficialRegime := officialRegime
    if regimeCandidate == lastCandidate
        regimeStreak := regimeStreak + 1
    else
        lastCandidate := regimeCandidate
        regimeStreak := 1
    if regimeStreak >= persistenceBars
        officialRegime := regimeCandidate

isDirectionalTrend(r) => r == "BULL_TREND" or r == "BEAR_TREND"

// ── Session classification (context only — never gates a decision) ───────
utcHour = hour(time, "UTC")
session = (utcHour >= asiaStartUtc and utcHour < londonStartUtc) ? "ASIA" :
     (utcHour >= londonStartUtc and utcHour < nyStartUtc) ? "LONDON" :
     (utcHour >= nyStartUtc and utcHour < otherStartUtc) ? "NEW_YORK" :
     "OTHER"

// =============================================================================
// STRUCTURE ENGINE (P2, REVISED in the P2 review/fix pass) — confirmed
// pivots, HH/HL/LH/LL, split close/wick born-consumed protection, a bounded
// multi-level structural retention store, BOS/CHoCH, sweeps, PDH/PDL,
// displacement, structure direction, and an anchored structural range.
// =============================================================================

// ── Confirmed pivots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ta.pivothigh/ta.pivotlow are Pine's own non-repaint pivot primitives: a
// pivot at physical bar (bar_index - pivotRightBars) only becomes non-na
// HERE, on the bar where all `pivotRightBars` confirming bars have already
// closed. Location bar and confirmation bar are therefore ALWAYS distinct
// (confirmBar = location + pivotRightBars) and are tracked as two separate
// fields below — never conflated.
pivotHighVal = ta.pivothigh(pivotLeftBars, pivotRightBars)
pivotLowVal  = ta.pivotlow(pivotLeftBars, pivotRightBars)

// ── Born-consumed protection: CLOSE vs WICK, explicitly separated ────────
// (P2 review fix — a prior version checked only CLOSE-based consumption and
// asserted, without proof, that this covered "born consumed" entirely.)
//
// The UNKNOWABLE interval for a pivot at physical bar P confirmed at bar
// C = P + pivotRightBars is the OPEN range of bars (P, C) — i.e. bars
// P+1 .. C-1 (length pivotRightBars-1). Bar P itself is the pivot's own
// location bar (already known the moment it happens, not "unknowable"), and
// bar C is the confirmation bar itself (evaluated separately, not part of
// the gap). A prior version's window inadvertently included bar P; fixed
// here to cover exactly P+1..C-1.
//
// Two DISTINCT questions are asked over that exact window, using `high`/
// `low` (relevant to WICK/sweep semantics — a level whose wick was already
// touched during the unknowable window must never later masquerade as a
// fresh sweep) and `close` (relevant to BOS/CHoCH semantics — a level
// already validly closed-through during the unknowable window must never
// later fire a fake first BOS/CHoCH) separately:
//   bornWickInteractedHigh/Low — did HIGH/LOW already cross the level?
//   bornCloseConsumedHigh/Low  — did CLOSE already cross the level?
// (close-consumed implies wick-interacted, never the reverse.)
//
// PROOF both are structurally impossible for NATIVE ta.pivothigh/pivotlow —
// not merely asserted: ta.pivothigh(left,right) requires EVERY one of the
// `right` confirming bars to have a HIGH strictly LOWER than the pivot's
// high (mirrored for pivotlow / LOW). That is the pivot definition itself —
// if any confirming bar's high were >= the candidate, that candidate simply
// would not confirm as a pivot at bar C in the first place. So within
// P+1..C-1, every bar's HIGH < pivotHigh — and since CLOSE <= HIGH for the
// same bar, every one of those bars' CLOSE < pivotHigh too. Both checks are
// therefore provably always false for this specific pivot source. They are
// implemented anyway, split and named explicitly, as tested defense-in-
// depth against a future change (e.g. a different pivot/level source that
// does not carry the same built-in guarantee) — never trusted implicitly.
gapLen = math.max(pivotRightBars - 1, 1)   // ta.highest/lowest need length >= 1; gated by hasConfirmGap below
hasConfirmGap = pivotRightBars > 1          // false when rightBars=1 (no bars physically exist between P and C)

// Called unconditionally every bar (compiler requirement for history-
// referencing functions) — offset by [1] so the window is exactly
// bars C-1 .. C-gapLen = P+1 .. C-1, EXCLUDING the pivot's own location bar.
gapHighestHigh  = ta.highest(high[1], gapLen)
gapLowestLow    = ta.lowest(low[1], gapLen)
gapHighestClose = ta.highest(close[1], gapLen)
gapLowestClose  = ta.lowest(close[1], gapLen)

bornWickInteractedHigh = not na(pivotHighVal) and hasConfirmGap and gapHighestHigh  > pivotHighVal
bornWickInteractedLow  = not na(pivotLowVal)  and hasConfirmGap and gapLowestLow    < pivotLowVal
bornCloseConsumedHigh  = not na(pivotHighVal) and hasConfirmGap and gapHighestClose > pivotHighVal
bornCloseConsumedLow   = not na(pivotLowVal)  and hasConfirmGap and gapLowestClose  < pivotLowVal

// ── Bounded active structural level storage (P2 review fix) ──────────────
// A prior version tracked only the SINGLE most recent confirmed swing per
// side, silently discarding an older, still-unbroken, structurally relevant
// level the moment a newer pivot confirmed — so a later close that broke
// the OLDER level would never be detected. Fixed with a small, BOUNDED
// (never unlimited) FIFO store per side: up to `maxActiveLevels` levels are
// retained until each is individually retired (see below), not merely
// superseded by recency.
//
// Documented supersession/invalidation rule (the ONLY ways a level ever
// leaves the active store):
//   1. CONSUMED — its close was validly broken (BOS/CHoCH fired for it).
//   2. SWEPT — for sweep-eligibility purposes only; a swept-but-not-closed
//      level remains active for a LATER genuine close-based break.
//   3. CAPACITY EVICTION — if adding a new level would exceed
//      `maxActiveLevels`, the OLDEST active entry (by confirmBar, FIFO) is
//      evicted. This is the one deliberate, bounded-memory trade-off: if
//      more than `maxActiveLevels` levels are simultaneously unconsumed,
//      the very oldest is dropped rather than growing storage without
//      limit. Documented explicitly, not silent.
type StructLevel
    float  price
    string kind                 // HH/LH/EQH or HL/LL/EQL
    int    locationBar
    int    confirmBar
    bool   bornCloseConsumed
    bool   bornWickInteracted
    bool   consumed             // retired: already generated its one BOS/CHoCH
    bool   swept                // retired-for-sweep: already generated its one sweep

var array<StructLevel> activeHighLevels = array.new<StructLevel>()
var array<StructLevel> activeLowLevels  = array.new<StructLevel>()

// ── Swing identity + HH/HL/LH/LL classification ───────────────────────────
// Classification (HH/LH/EQH, HL/LL/EQL) is UNCHANGED from the prior version:
// a new pivot classifies itself against the single PREVIOUS tracked swing of
// the same type, written exactly once at its own confirmation bar, and that
// classification is never revisited later. `lastSwingHigh`/`lastSwingLow`
// (and friends) remain simple "most recent" mirrors for the contract/debug
// tables; the array above is what BOS/CHoCH/sweep detection actually uses.
var float  lastSwingHigh             = na
var string lastSwingHighType         = "NA"
var int    lastSwingHighBar          = na
var int    lastSwingHighConfirmBar   = na
var bool   lastSwingHighBornConsumed = false   // mirrors bornCloseConsumed for the most recent level
var float  prevSwingHighForCompare   = na

var float  lastSwingLow              = na
var string lastSwingLowType          = "NA"
var int    lastSwingLowBar           = na
var int    lastSwingLowConfirmBar    = na
var bool   lastSwingLowBornConsumed  = false
var float  prevSwingLowForCompare    = na

if confirmedBar and not na(pivotHighVal)
    swingTol = atrVal * swingEqAtrMult
    newHighType = na(prevSwingHighForCompare) ? "HH" :
         (pivotHighVal - prevSwingHighForCompare > swingTol) ? "HH" :
         (pivotHighVal - prevSwingHighForCompare < -swingTol) ? "LH" :
         "EQH"
    prevSwingHighForCompare := pivotHighVal
    lastSwingHigh := pivotHighVal
    lastSwingHighType := newHighType
    lastSwingHighBar := bar_index - pivotRightBars
    lastSwingHighConfirmBar := bar_index
    lastSwingHighBornConsumed := bornCloseConsumedHigh

    newHighLevel = StructLevel.new(pivotHighVal, newHighType, bar_index - pivotRightBars, bar_index, bornCloseConsumedHigh, bornWickInteractedHigh, bornCloseConsumedHigh, bornWickInteractedHigh)
    array.push(activeHighLevels, newHighLevel)
    if array.size(activeHighLevels) > maxActiveLevels
        array.shift(activeHighLevels)  // documented FIFO capacity eviction — see rule 3 above

if confirmedBar and not na(pivotLowVal)
    swingTolL = atrVal * swingEqAtrMult
    newLowType = na(prevSwingLowForCompare) ? "HL" :
         (pivotLowVal - prevSwingLowForCompare > swingTolL) ? "HL" :
         (pivotLowVal - prevSwingLowForCompare < -swingTolL) ? "LL" :
         "EQL"
    prevSwingLowForCompare := pivotLowVal
    lastSwingLow := pivotLowVal
    lastSwingLowType := newLowType
    lastSwingLowBar := bar_index - pivotRightBars
    lastSwingLowConfirmBar := bar_index
    lastSwingLowBornConsumed := bornCloseConsumedLow

    newLowLevel = StructLevel.new(pivotLowVal, newLowType, bar_index - pivotRightBars, bar_index, bornCloseConsumedLow, bornWickInteractedLow, bornCloseConsumedLow, bornWickInteractedLow)
    array.push(activeLowLevels, newLowLevel)
    if array.size(activeLowLevels) > maxActiveLevels
        array.shift(activeLowLevels)

// ── BOS / CHoCH / sweep detection over the bounded active-level store ────
// structureDirection is deterministic and INDEPENDENT of officialRegime
// (EMA-based) — see §14 of the P2 spec. 3 states (BULLISH/BEARISH/NEUTRAL):
// the first-ever break from NEUTRAL establishes structure via BOS (no prior
// "character" to change away from); only a break AGAINST an established
// direction counts as CHoCH.
//
// LEVEL-SELECTION PRIORITY (P2 review fix, §3/§4): a single confirmed bar
// can cross more than one retained active level on the same side. Exactly
// ONE authoritative semantic event fires per side per bar — the level with
// the MOST RECENT confirmBar among those actually crossed (most immediately
// relevant to current structure). Every OTHER active level also genuinely
// crossed by this same bar is retired (marked consumed/swept) so it can
// never later re-fire, but does not generate its own separate event.
//
// Dedup / lifecycle: each level fires AT MOST ONE sweep event and AT MOST
// ONE break (BOS/CHoCH) event during its lifetime in the store — the
// `.consumed`/`.swept` flags latch true and are checked before a level is
// even considered eligible.
//
// Chronology guard: a level can only be evaluated for a break/sweep on bars
// STRICTLY AFTER its own confirmBar (`bar_index > level.confirmBar`) — the
// bar that confirms a level is never also treated as "the break bar" of
// that same level.
var string structureDirection    = "NEUTRAL"   // BULLISH / BEARISH / NEUTRAL
var string lastStructureEvent    = "NONE"
var int    lastStructureEventBar = na
var string lastBosDirection      = "NA"
var int    lastBosBar            = na
var string lastChochDirection    = "NA"
var int    lastChochBar          = na
var string lastSweepType         = "NA"
var int    lastSweepBar          = na

if confirmedBar
    // ── HIGH side ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    int authHighBreakIdx = -1
    int authHighBreakConfirmBar = -1
    // P4B runtime-safety patch: Pine's `for` loop auto-reverses direction
    // when `to < from` (which happens whenever the array is empty, since
    // `size - 1 == -1`), and does NOT execute zero times in that case — it
    // executes for i = 0 and i = -1, calling array.get() on an out-of-bounds
    // index. Every loop below is guarded by an explicit `array.size(...) > 0`
    // check so an empty array is never indexed at all. This is a pure
    // runtime-safety guard: when the array has 1+ elements, behavior,
    // iteration order, and priority/consumption/sweep logic are all
    // byte-for-byte identical to before this patch.
    if array.size(activeHighLevels) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(activeHighLevels) - 1
            lvl = array.get(activeHighLevels, i)
            if not lvl.consumed and bar_index > lvl.confirmBar and close > lvl.price and lvl.confirmBar > authHighBreakConfirmBar
                authHighBreakConfirmBar := lvl.confirmBar
                authHighBreakIdx := i

    if authHighBreakIdx >= 0
        highEvent = structureDirection == "BEARISH" ? "BULLISH_CHOCH" : "BULLISH_BOS"
        lastStructureEvent := highEvent
        lastStructureEventBar := bar_index
        if highEvent == "BULLISH_BOS"
            lastBosDirection := "BULLISH"
            lastBosBar := bar_index
        else
            lastChochDirection := "BULLISH"
            lastChochBar := bar_index
        structureDirection := "BULLISH"
        // Retire EVERY active high level this same close genuinely broke —
        // not just the authoritative one — so none can re-fire later.
        if array.size(activeHighLevels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(activeHighLevels) - 1
                lvl2 = array.get(activeHighLevels, i)
                if not lvl2.consumed and bar_index > lvl2.confirmBar and close > lvl2.price
                    lvl2.consumed := true   // UDT is a reference type — mutates the stored object directly
    else
        int authHighSweepIdx = -1
        int authHighSweepConfirmBar = -1
        if array.size(activeHighLevels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(activeHighLevels) - 1
                lvl = array.get(activeHighLevels, i)
                if not lvl.consumed and not lvl.swept and bar_index > lvl.confirmBar and high > lvl.price and lvl.confirmBar > authHighSweepConfirmBar
                    authHighSweepConfirmBar := lvl.confirmBar
                    authHighSweepIdx := i
        if authHighSweepIdx >= 0
            lastSweepType := "SWEEP_HIGH"
            lastSweepBar := bar_index
            if array.size(activeHighLevels) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(activeHighLevels) - 1
                    lvl2 = array.get(activeHighLevels, i)
                    if not lvl2.consumed and not lvl2.swept and bar_index > lvl2.confirmBar and high > lvl2.price
                        lvl2.swept := true

    // ── LOW side (mirror) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    int authLowBreakIdx = -1
    int authLowBreakConfirmBar = -1
    if array.size(activeLowLevels) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(activeLowLevels) - 1
            lvl = array.get(activeLowLevels, i)
            if not lvl.consumed and bar_index > lvl.confirmBar and close < lvl.price and lvl.confirmBar > authLowBreakConfirmBar
                authLowBreakConfirmBar := lvl.confirmBar
                authLowBreakIdx := i

    if authLowBreakIdx >= 0
        lowEvent = structureDirection == "BULLISH" ? "BEARISH_CHOCH" : "BEARISH_BOS"
        lastStructureEvent := lowEvent
        lastStructureEventBar := bar_index
        if lowEvent == "BEARISH_BOS"
            lastBosDirection := "BEARISH"
            lastBosBar := bar_index
        else
            lastChochDirection := "BEARISH"
            lastChochBar := bar_index
        structureDirection := "BEARISH"
        if array.size(activeLowLevels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(activeLowLevels) - 1
                lvl2 = array.get(activeLowLevels, i)
                if not lvl2.consumed and bar_index > lvl2.confirmBar and close < lvl2.price
                    lvl2.consumed := true
    else
        int authLowSweepIdx = -1
        int authLowSweepConfirmBar = -1
        if array.size(activeLowLevels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(activeLowLevels) - 1
                lvl = array.get(activeLowLevels, i)
                if not lvl.consumed and not lvl.swept and bar_index > lvl.confirmBar and low < lvl.price and lvl.confirmBar > authLowSweepConfirmBar
                    authLowSweepConfirmBar := lvl.confirmBar
                    authLowSweepIdx := i
        if authLowSweepIdx >= 0
            lastSweepType := "SWEEP_LOW"
            lastSweepBar := bar_index
            if array.size(activeLowLevels) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(activeLowLevels) - 1
                    lvl2 = array.get(activeLowLevels, i)
                    if not lvl2.consumed and not lvl2.swept and bar_index > lvl2.confirmBar and low < lvl2.price
                        lvl2.swept := true

// ── PDH / PDL (confirmed previous day only) ───────────────────────────────
// `high[1]`/`low[1]` INSIDE the daily security context is the same
// non-repaint pattern used for HTF above: it is always the PRIOR, fully
// completed daily bar's high/low — never the current, still-forming day's
// running high/low. No current-day leakage is possible.
pdh = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", high[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
pdl = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", low[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

var float  trackedPdh          = na
var float  trackedPdl          = na
var bool   pdhSweptForValue    = false
var bool   pdlSweptForValue    = false
var string lastDailySweep      = "NA"
var int    lastDailySweepBar   = na

if confirmedBar
    // A new PDH/PDL value (i.e. a new calendar day rolled over) resets that
    // side's one-sweep-per-value eligibility.
    if pdh != trackedPdh
        trackedPdh := pdh
        pdhSweptForValue := false
    if pdl != trackedPdl
        trackedPdl := pdl
        pdlSweptForValue := false

    if not na(pdh) and not pdhSweptForValue and high > pdh and close <= pdh
        lastDailySweep := "PDH_SWEEP"
        lastDailySweepBar := bar_index
        pdhSweptForValue := true

    if not na(pdl) and not pdlSweptForValue and low < pdl and close >= pdl
        lastDailySweep := "PDL_SWEEP"
        lastDailySweepBar := bar_index
        pdlSweptForValue := true

// ── Displacement (normalized, not "big candle") ───────────────────────────
bodySize   = math.abs(close - open)
rangeSize  = high - low
bodyRatio  = rangeSize > 0 ? bodySize / rangeSize : 0.0
closeLoc   = rangeSize > 0 ? (close - low) / rangeSize : 0.5   // 0 = at low, 1 = at high
bigBody    = bodySize >= displacementAtrMult * atrVal
bullishDisplacement = bigBody and close > open and bodyRatio >= displacementBodyRatioMin and closeLoc >= displacementCloseLocMin
bearishDisplacement = bigBody and close < open and bodyRatio >= displacementBodyRatioMin and closeLoc <= (1.0 - displacementCloseLocMin)
displacementState = bullishDisplacement ? "BULLISH_DISPLACEMENT" : bearishDisplacement ? "BEARISH_DISPLACEMENT" : "NONE"

// ── Anchored structural range ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Distinct from the ROLLING compression/range candidate detection used by
// the regime engine above. A range only becomes ANCHORED (boundaries
// frozen) after `rangeAnchorPersistBars` CONSECUTIVE CONFIRMED bars of
// COMPRESSION/RANGE regime — at that point rangeHigh/rangeLow are set once
// and never move again while this range identity is ACTIVE or BROKEN. A
// genuine breakout terminates it; the NEXT anchor creates a brand-new
// identity rather than rewriting this one's boundaries.
var string rangeState        = "NONE"   // NONE / ACTIVE / BROKEN
var float  rangeHigh         = na
var float  rangeLow          = na
var int    rangeAnchorBar    = na
var int    rangeConfirmBar   = na
var int    rangeId           = 0
var int    rangeRegimeStreak = 0

// Called unconditionally every bar (compiler requirement for
// history-referencing functions) and only USED at the moment of anchoring.
candidateRangeHigh = ta.highest(high, rangeAnchorPersistBars)
candidateRangeLow  = ta.lowest(low, rangeAnchorPersistBars)

if confirmedBar
    if officialRegime == "COMPRESSION" or officialRegime == "RANGE"
        rangeRegimeStreak := rangeRegimeStreak + 1
    else
        rangeRegimeStreak := 0

    if rangeState != "ACTIVE" and rangeRegimeStreak >= rangeAnchorPersistBars
        rangeHigh := candidateRangeHigh
        rangeLow := candidateRangeLow
        rangeAnchorBar := bar_index - rangeAnchorPersistBars + 1
        rangeConfirmBar := bar_index
        rangeId := rangeId + 1
        rangeState := "ACTIVE"

    // Chronology guard: breakout can only be evaluated strictly AFTER the
    // range's own confirmation bar — never on the anchoring bar itself.
    if rangeState == "ACTIVE" and bar_index > rangeConfirmBar
        if close > rangeHigh or close < rangeLow
            rangeState := "BROKEN"
            rangeRegimeStreak := 0  // force a fresh persistence count before any NEW range can anchor

// =============================================================================
// CORRECTION ENGINE (P1, EXTENDED in P2 with structural evidence) —
// persistent state machine, confirmed-bar gated.
// =============================================================================
var bool   correctionActive   = false
var string correctionSide     = "NA"      // "BULL" (correcting a bull trend) or "BEAR"
var int    corrStartBar       = na
var int    corrStartTime      = na
var string correctionEvidence = "NA"
var bool   correctionResolved = false     // transient: true only on the bar it resolves
var int    corrResolvedBar    = na        // audit trail — preserved across future corrections
var string corrResolvedSide   = "NA"      // audit trail — preserved across future corrections
var int    corrRecoverStreak  = 0

// Swing anchors use ONLY prior, already-closed bars (`high[1]`/`low[1]` as
// the series root) — the current, possibly-still-forming bar's extreme can
// never itself become the correction-displacement anchor.
recentSwingHigh = ta.highest(high[1], swingLookback)
recentSwingLow  = ta.lowest(low[1], swingLookback)

// P2: a freshly confirmed, matching-direction structural event is
// additional, independent activation/recovery evidence alongside P1's
// existing EMA-based evidence — never a replacement for it, and never
// sufficient on its own to SKIP the multi-bar recovery-confirmation streak
// required for resolution (see the resolution block below).
freshBearishStructureThisBar = lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and (lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_CHOCH" or lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_BOS")
freshBullishStructureThisBar = lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and (lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_CHOCH" or lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_BOS")

if confirmedBar
    correctionResolved := false // reset the transient one-bar-only flag every confirmed bar

    // Trend-side flip (BULL_TREND <-> BEAR_TREND directly): the correction
    // context no longer means anything relative to the new direction, so
    // fully reset the transient fields. The audit trail
    // (corrResolvedBar/corrResolvedSide) is left untouched on purpose.
    if isDirectionalTrend(officialRegime) and isDirectionalTrend(priorOfficialRegime) and officialRegime != priorOfficialRegime
        correctionActive := false
        correctionSide := "NA"
        corrStartBar := na
        corrStartTime := na
        correctionEvidence := "NA"
        corrRecoverStreak := 0

    // Leaving directional trend context entirely (e.g. into RANGE/CHOP/
    // COMPRESSION/TRANSITION/HIGH_VOLATILITY) while a correction was active:
    // clear the now-meaningless transient correction state. This is NOT a
    // resolution — corrResolvedBar/corrResolvedSide are left untouched.
    if correctionActive and not isDirectionalTrend(officialRegime)
        correctionActive := false
        correctionSide := "NA"
        corrStartBar := na
        corrStartTime := na
        correctionEvidence := "NA"
        corrRecoverStreak := 0

    // ── Activation — only from a valid directional context. Either P1's
    // original two-piece evidence (structural displacement vs swing anchor
    // + EMA momentum fading), OR a freshly confirmed matching-direction
    // structural event (itself already a rigorously confirmed, non-
    // arbitrary piece of evidence) — never a single arbitrary candle. ─────
    if not correctionActive and officialRegime == "BULL_TREND"
        displacementVsSwing = recentSwingHigh - close
        momentumFading = emaFast < emaFast[corrMomentumLookback]
        emaEvidence = displacementVsSwing >= corrAtrMultiplier * atrVal and momentumFading
        if emaEvidence or freshBearishStructureThisBar
            correctionActive := true
            correctionSide := "BULL"
            corrStartBar := bar_index
            corrStartTime := time
            correctionEvidence := emaEvidence ? "displacement_vs_swing_high+ema_fast_declining" : "structural_bearish_break"
            corrRecoverStreak := 0

    if not correctionActive and officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND"
        displacementVsSwingL = close - recentSwingLow
        momentumFadingL = emaFast > emaFast[corrMomentumLookback]
        emaEvidenceL = displacementVsSwingL >= corrAtrMultiplier * atrVal and momentumFadingL
        if emaEvidenceL or freshBullishStructureThisBar
            correctionActive := true
            correctionSide := "BEAR"
            corrStartBar := bar_index
            corrStartTime := time
            correctionEvidence := emaEvidenceL ? "displacement_vs_swing_low+ema_fast_rising" : "structural_bullish_break"
            corrRecoverStreak := 0

    // ── Resolution — CHRONOLOGY-PROTECTED: strictly requires
    // bar_index > corrStartBar (never the activation bar itself), plus
    // multiple consecutive confirmed bars of recovery evidence (never a
    // single tick — a fresh matching structural event on its own bar counts
    // as evidence FOR that one bar, it does not shortcut the streak), and
    // can only use information knowable as of THIS confirmed bar — no
    // future pivot, no backdating. ─────────────────────────────────────────
    if correctionActive and bar_index > corrStartBar
        recoveredEma = correctionSide == "BULL" ? (close > emaFast) : (correctionSide == "BEAR" ? (close < emaFast) : false)
        recoveredStructure = correctionSide == "BULL" ? freshBullishStructureThisBar : (correctionSide == "BEAR" ? freshBearishStructureThisBar : false)
        recovered = recoveredEma or recoveredStructure
        if recovered
            corrRecoverStreak := corrRecoverStreak + 1
        else
            corrRecoverStreak := 0

        if corrRecoverStreak >= corrResolveConfirmBars
            correctionResolved := true
            corrResolvedBar := bar_index
            corrResolvedSide := correctionSide
            correctionActive := false
            correctionSide := "NA"
            corrStartBar := na
            corrStartTime := na
            correctionEvidence := "NA"
            corrRecoverStreak := 0

correctionStateStr = correctionActive ? "ACTIVE" : "NONE"

// =============================================================================
// DECISION ENGINE (P3) — the first phase authorized to reach BUY/SELL.
//
// Pipeline (§2 of the P3 spec): REGIME → STRUCTURE → IS TRADING APPROPRIATE?
// → MODEL ELIGIBILITY → SETUP → CORRECTION BLOCKER → TRIGGER → CONFIRMATION
// → ENTRY LOCATION → QUALITY GATE → LOGICAL STOP → LOGICAL TARGETS →
// RR VALIDATION → FINAL ACTION. Every gate below can only ever narrow the
// outcome toward WAIT — none can loosen, repair, or manufacture a result.
// =============================================================================

// ── Shared structural-anchor helpers ──────────────────────────────────────
// Nearest ACTIVE (not yet consumed) level in `store` beyond `refPrice`, in
// the given direction — used for both SL anchoring (nearest opposing-side
// level = invalidation point) and TP2 objective (nearest same-side-as-
// direction level beyond entry = realistic structural target). Reuses the
// P2 bounded active-level arrays directly; never invents a level.
f_nearestAbove(store, refPrice) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(store) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(store) - 1
            lvl = array.get(store, i)
            if not lvl.consumed and lvl.price > refPrice and (na(best) or lvl.price < best)
                best := lvl.price
    best

f_nearestBelow(store, refPrice) =>
    float best = na
    if array.size(store) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(store) - 1
            lvl = array.get(store, i)
            if not lvl.consumed and lvl.price < refPrice and (na(best) or lvl.price > best)
                best := lvl.price
    best

// ── §4 Regime × Model × Direction eligibility matrix (documented, exact) ──
// HIGH_VOLATILITY: explicitly gated OFF for every model — "do not assume
// volatility means opportunity" (§25). No model is currently approved to
// trade through it; a later phase may add explicit extra-confirmation
// handling, but P3 does not.
// COMPRESSION: eligible for BO only (breakout/retest architecture) — never
// TC/PB/MR/SR, since compression has no established trend or range to
// pull back from or mean-revert within yet.
// CORRECTION: correctionActive is a regime-independent hard blocker,
// checked separately below — it is never encoded as a "regime" here.
tcLongEligible  = officialRegime == "BULL_TREND"
tcShortEligible = officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND"
pbLongEligible  = officialRegime == "BULL_TREND"
pbShortEligible = officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND"
boLongEligible  = officialRegime == "BULL_TREND" or officialRegime == "RANGE" or officialRegime == "COMPRESSION"
boShortEligible = officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND" or officialRegime == "RANGE" or officialRegime == "COMPRESSION"
mrLongEligible  = officialRegime == "RANGE"   // MR blocked in every trend regime, per §10 — RANGE only
mrShortEligible = officialRegime == "RANGE"
srLongEligible  = officialRegime == "BULL_TREND" or officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND" or officialRegime == "RANGE"
srShortEligible = officialRegime == "BULL_TREND" or officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND" or officialRegime == "RANGE"

// ── TC — Trend Continuation ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup: structure direction already agrees with the trend AND a matching
// displacement occurred recently (trend alone is never a setup by itself).
// Trigger: a FRESH continuation BOS in the trend direction (CHoCH would
// mean the trend is changing character, not continuing — never a TC
// trigger). Anchor (SL basis / overextension reference): the most recent
// tracked swing on the opposing side.
barsSinceBullishDisp = ta.barssince(displacementState == "BULLISH_DISPLACEMENT")
barsSinceBearishDisp = ta.barssince(displacementState == "BEARISH_DISPLACEMENT")

tcLongSetupReady  = tcLongEligible  and not correctionActive and structureDirection == "BULLISH" and not na(barsSinceBullishDisp) and barsSinceBullishDisp <= tcSetupLookback
tcShortSetupReady = tcShortEligible and not correctionActive and structureDirection == "BEARISH" and not na(barsSinceBearishDisp) and barsSinceBearishDisp <= tcSetupLookback
tcLongTrigger  = tcLongSetupReady  and lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_BOS"
tcShortTrigger = tcShortSetupReady and lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_BOS"
tcLongAnchor  = lastSwingLow
tcShortAnchor = lastSwingHigh

// ── PB — Trend Pullback ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup: the trend's correction resolved RECENTLY (not stale) and
// correctionActive is currently false — resolution alone is never a setup;
// it only PERMITS looking for one (§8). Trigger: a fresh matching-direction
// continuation BOS or "back with trend" CHoCH, strictly after the
// resolution bar. Anchor: the pullback's own low/high — approximated by the
// most recent tracked swing, which is the pullback extreme itself in the
// common case (the correction's retracement swing).
pbLongSetupReady  = pbLongEligible  and not correctionActive and not na(corrResolvedBar) and corrResolvedSide == "BULL" and (bar_index - corrResolvedBar) <= pbSetupLookback
pbShortSetupReady = pbShortEligible and not correctionActive and not na(corrResolvedBar) and corrResolvedSide == "BEAR" and (bar_index - corrResolvedBar) <= pbSetupLookback
pbLongTrigger  = pbLongSetupReady  and lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEventBar > corrResolvedBar and (lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_BOS" or lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_CHOCH")
pbShortTrigger = pbShortSetupReady and lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEventBar > corrResolvedBar and (lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_BOS" or lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_CHOCH")
pbLongAnchor  = lastSwingLow
pbShortAnchor = lastSwingHigh

// ── BO — Breakout / Retest ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup: the P2 anchored range must have already been confirmed BEFORE any
// breakout (reusing P2's own chronology-protected rangeState/rangeConfirmBar
// directly — never a fresh ad-hoc breakout check).
//
// P3 review §3 fix: BREAKOUT, RETEST, and RECLAIM are now three explicitly
// DISTINCT bars, never collapsible into one. A prior version could satisfy
// the retest touch and the reclaim close on the SAME candle (setting
// `boLongRetested := true` and then, on that identical bar's continued
// script execution, `boLongTrigger` immediately reading the just-updated
// flag). Fixed by recording the retest's OWN bar (`boLongRetestBar`) and
// requiring the reclaim to occur STRICTLY AFTER it — so:
//   breakout bar (boLongBar) < retest bar (boLongRetestBar) < reclaim bar
// is enforced by construction, never merely by convention.
// Deterministic invalidation: if price closes back THROUGH the broken
// boundary (beyond the ATR tolerance, in the wrong direction) after a
// retest was already recorded, the sequence is invalidated outright —
// a failed retest does not linger indefinitely waiting for a reclaim that
// contradicts what the retest just showed. Pending sequences also expire
// after boRetestMaxBars measured from the breakout bar.
var string priorRangeState  = "NONE"
var bool  boLongActive      = false
var float boLongLevel       = na
var int   boLongBar         = na       // breakout bar
var bool  boLongRetested    = false
var int   boLongRetestBar   = na       // retest bar — always > boLongBar
var bool  boShortActive     = false
var float boShortLevel      = na
var int   boShortBar        = na
var bool  boShortRetested   = false
var int   boShortRetestBar  = na

if confirmedBar
    if rangeState == "BROKEN" and priorRangeState == "ACTIVE"
        if close > rangeHigh
            boLongActive := true
            boLongLevel := rangeHigh
            boLongBar := bar_index
            boLongRetested := false
            boLongRetestBar := na
        else if close < rangeLow
            boShortActive := true
            boShortLevel := rangeLow
            boShortBar := bar_index
            boShortRetested := false
            boShortRetestBar := na
    priorRangeState := rangeState

    if boLongActive and (bar_index - boLongBar) > boRetestMaxBars
        boLongActive := false   // expired — no retest arrived in time
    // Retest: only on a bar STRICTLY AFTER the breakout bar.
    if boLongActive and not boLongRetested and bar_index > boLongBar and low <= boLongLevel + boRetestAtrTol * atrVal
        boLongRetested := true
        boLongRetestBar := bar_index
    // Retest failure: after a retest was recorded, price closes back
    // through the broken boundary (beyond tolerance) rather than holding —
    // invalidate rather than leave the sequence dangling.
    if boLongActive and boLongRetested and bar_index > boLongRetestBar and close < boLongLevel - boRetestAtrTol * atrVal
        boLongActive := false

    if boShortActive and (bar_index - boShortBar) > boRetestMaxBars
        boShortActive := false
    if boShortActive and not boShortRetested and bar_index > boShortBar and high >= boShortLevel - boRetestAtrTol * atrVal
        boShortRetested := true
        boShortRetestBar := bar_index
    if boShortActive and boShortRetested and bar_index > boShortRetestBar and close > boShortLevel + boRetestAtrTol * atrVal
        boShortActive := false

boLongSetupReady  = boLongEligible  and not correctionActive and boLongActive
boShortSetupReady = boShortEligible and not correctionActive and boShortActive
// Reclaim trigger: STRICTLY after the retest bar — never the retest bar
// itself, never the breakout bar.
boLongTrigger  = boLongSetupReady  and boLongRetested  and not na(boLongRetestBar)  and bar_index > boLongRetestBar  and close > boLongLevel
boShortTrigger = boShortSetupReady and boShortRetested and not na(boShortRetestBar) and bar_index > boShortRetestBar and close < boShortLevel
boLongAnchor  = boLongLevel
boShortAnchor = boShortLevel

// ── MR — Mean Reversion ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup: RANGE regime only (hard-blocked in every trend regime, §10).
// Trigger (P3 review §1 fix): price must GENUINELY WICK BEYOND the anchored
// range boundary AND close back INSIDE it this same confirmed bar — every
// condition is written EXPLICITLY and self-contained directly on the
// trigger line (never relying only on mrLongSetupReady's own low/high
// check, which a future edit to that variable could otherwise silently
// decouple from). Concretely, for LONG: `low <= rangeLow` (a genuine touch
// or undercut — not merely "close" to it) AND `close > rangeLow` (closed
// back inside) AND the overshoot `(rangeLow - low)` bounded by the ATR
// tolerance. Because `low <= rangeLow` is now required explicitly and
// unconditionally on this line, a candle that stays entirely ABOVE
// rangeLow (never touching it) makes `rangeLow - low` NEGATIVE, but the
// mandatory `low <= rangeLow` term independently fails first — so a
// negative overshoot value can never satisfy this condition on its own.
//
// Opposing-displacement blocker: MR must never fade a genuine breakout — a
// STRONG opposing displacement within the last `mrDisplacementBlockBars`
// bars (not just this exact candle) blocks the setup entirely, reusing the
// existing P2 `barsSinceBullishDisp`/`barsSinceBearishDisp` series computed
// above for TC — no new indicator is introduced.
mrLongDisplacementBlocked  = not na(barsSinceBearishDisp) and barsSinceBearishDisp <= mrDisplacementBlockBars
mrShortDisplacementBlocked = not na(barsSinceBullishDisp) and barsSinceBullishDisp <= mrDisplacementBlockBars

mrLongSetupReady  = mrLongEligible  and not correctionActive and not na(rangeLow)  and rangeState == "ACTIVE" and low  <= rangeLow and not mrLongDisplacementBlocked
mrShortSetupReady = mrShortEligible and not correctionActive and not na(rangeHigh) and rangeState == "ACTIVE" and high >= rangeHigh and not mrShortDisplacementBlocked
mrLongTrigger  = mrLongSetupReady  and low  <= rangeLow  and close > rangeLow  and (rangeLow - low)   <= mrBoundaryAtrTol * atrVal and not mrLongDisplacementBlocked
mrShortTrigger = mrShortSetupReady and high >= rangeHigh and close < rangeHigh and (high - rangeHigh) <= mrBoundaryAtrTol * atrVal and not mrShortDisplacementBlocked
mrLongAnchor  = low    // the sweep bar's own low is the invalidation reference
mrShortAnchor = high

// ── SR — Structure / Rejection ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Setup: any regime where structure is meaningful (not COMPRESSION/
// TRANSITION/CHOP/HIGH_VOLATILITY). Trigger requires one of the SAME
// deterministic, already-confirmed P2 events used elsewhere — never a bare
// wick: a genuine swing-level sweep, a PDH/PDL sweep, or a CHoCH — firing
// on THIS confirmed bar. One wick alone (without a P2-confirmed sweep
// event) is never sufficient.
srLongSetupReady  = srLongEligible  and not correctionActive
srShortSetupReady = srShortEligible and not correctionActive
srLongTrigger  = srLongSetupReady  and ((lastSweepType == "SWEEP_LOW"  and lastSweepBar == bar_index) or (lastDailySweep == "PDL_SWEEP" and lastDailySweepBar == bar_index) or (lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_CHOCH"))
srShortTrigger = srShortSetupReady and ((lastSweepType == "SWEEP_HIGH" and lastSweepBar == bar_index) or (lastDailySweep == "PDH_SWEEP" and lastDailySweepBar == bar_index) or (lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_CHOCH"))
srLongAnchor  = lastSwingLow
srShortAnchor = lastSwingHigh

// ── §12 Model selection priority (documented, exact) ──────────────────────
// PB > BO > TC > MR > SR — a resolved trend correction is the most specific,
// highest-conviction context; an anchored breakout/retest is the next most
// structurally rigorous; plain continuation is common but least specific;
// range mean-reversion and structural rejection are the most opportunistic
// and sit last. Only the FIRST eligible model with a CONFIRMED TRIGGER this
// bar is ever considered — never more than one model per bar, never both
// directions.
anySetupReady = tcLongSetupReady or tcShortSetupReady or pbLongSetupReady or pbShortSetupReady or boLongSetupReady or boShortSetupReady or mrLongSetupReady or mrShortSetupReady or srLongSetupReady or srShortSetupReady
anyEligible = tcLongEligible or tcShortEligible or pbLongEligible or pbShortEligible or boLongEligible or boShortEligible or mrLongEligible or mrShortEligible or srLongEligible or srShortEligible

candModel  = pbLongTrigger or pbShortTrigger ? "PB" :
     boLongTrigger or boShortTrigger ? "BO" :
     tcLongTrigger or tcShortTrigger ? "TC" :
     mrLongTrigger or mrShortTrigger ? "MR" :
     srLongTrigger or srShortTrigger ? "SR" :
     "NA"
candIsLong = pbLongTrigger or boLongTrigger or tcLongTrigger or mrLongTrigger or srLongTrigger
candTriggered = candModel != "NA"
candAnchor = candModel == "PB" ? (candIsLong ? pbLongAnchor : pbShortAnchor) :
     candModel == "BO" ? (candIsLong ? boLongAnchor : boShortAnchor) :
     candModel == "TC" ? (candIsLong ? tcLongAnchor : tcShortAnchor) :
     candModel == "MR" ? (candIsLong ? mrLongAnchor : mrShortAnchor) :
     candModel == "SR" ? (candIsLong ? srLongAnchor : srShortAnchor) :
     na
// ── §16 Entry location: CHRONOLOGICAL staleness (P3 review §2 fix) ───────
// A prior version set `candTriggerBar = bar_index` unconditionally, making
// `candEntryLate` structurally always false — every trigger is "this bar"
// by definition, so comparing bar_index to itself can never exceed any
// positive threshold. That satisfied nothing.
//
// The fix distinguishes TWO different bars per model:
//   - candSetupOriginBar: when the underlying OPPORTUNITY first became
//     knowable (the displacement bar for TC, the resolution bar for PB,
//     the breakout bar for BO) — this can be, and usually is, OLDER than
//     the current bar.
//   - the current confirmed bar: when the TRIGGER itself fires.
// candEntryLate compares their gap against a threshold that is DELIBERATELY
// TIGHTER than each model's own setup-recency window (tcSetupLookback,
// pbSetupLookback, boRetestMaxBars) — so a trigger can be technically still
// "setup-ready" per that wider window yet independently flagged stale by
// this narrower one. This is what makes the gate genuinely reachable
// rather than vacuous (proven in tests/pine_p3_decision_model.test.js and
// tests/pine_p3_contract.test.js).
//
// MR and SR are same-bar by construction: their trigger conditions require
// the qualifying wick/sweep/CHoCH to occur on THIS confirmed bar (see their
// trigger definitions above) — there is no multi-bar setup-to-trigger gap
// to become stale. Their origin bar is therefore always bar_index, making
// `bar_index - candSetupOriginBar` always exactly 0, provably never late —
// documented here rather than silently relying on an unreachable generic
// gate (see the P3 review's explicit instruction).
tcOriginOffset = candIsLong ? barsSinceBullishDisp : barsSinceBearishDisp
candSetupOriginBar = candModel == "TC" ? (na(tcOriginOffset) ? na : bar_index - tcOriginOffset) :
     candModel == "PB" ? corrResolvedBar :
     candModel == "BO" ? (candIsLong ? boLongBar : boShortBar) :
     candModel == "MR" ? bar_index :
     candModel == "SR" ? bar_index :
     na
candMaxLateBars = candModel == "TC" ? tcMaxEntryLateBars :
     candModel == "PB" ? pbMaxEntryLateBars :
     candModel == "BO" ? boMaxEntryLateBars :
     0   // MR/SR: origin is always bar_index, so 0 > 0 is always false regardless of this value

// ── §5 (P3 review) Stale-event / duplicate-signal identity ────────────────
// SIGNAL_ID alone (model + side + bar_index) does not prove a NEW
// opportunity — bar_index changes every bar regardless of whether anything
// new actually happened. The real anti-recycling protection is that every
// model's OWN trigger condition already requires a fresh, this-bar
// confirmed event (see each model's trigger definition above: P2's
// consumed/swept latches prevent the same structural level firing twice,
// and `lastStructureEventBar == bar_index` / `lastSweepBar == bar_index`
// checks prevent an old event from re-qualifying on a later bar). This key
// adds one further, explicit, defense-in-depth layer: it identifies a
// candidate by its MODEL + DIRECTION + ORIGIN bar (not just the current
// bar), and a trade is only approved if that exact origin has never
// already produced an emitted signal — so even a hypothetical future
// change that let the same origin re-qualify across multiple bars could
// not silently emit a second signal from it.
candOriginKey = candTriggered and not na(candSetupOriginBar) ? candModel + "_" + (candIsLong ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH") + "_" + str.tostring(candSetupOriginBar) : "NA"

// ── §17 Entry semantics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ENTRY = the confirmed trigger bar's close. Never a historical idealized
// price unavailable at signal time, never a future bar's price.
candEntry = close

// ── §16 Entry location / do-not-chase (ATR-normalized, never raw dollars) ─
candOverextended = candTriggered and not na(candAnchor) and math.abs(candEntry - candAnchor) > overextendAtrMult * atrVal
candEntryLate = candTriggered and not na(candSetupOriginBar) and (bar_index - candSetupOriginBar) > candMaxLateBars
candLocationOk = candTriggered and not candOverextended and not candEntryLate

// ── §18/§19 Logical SL then targets, in order — never reverse-engineered ──
candIsValidDir = candTriggered and candLocationOk
slAnchor = candIsValidDir ? candAnchor : na
slRaw = na(slAnchor) ? (candIsLong ? candEntry - slAtrFallback * atrVal : candEntry + slAtrFallback * atrVal) : (candIsLong ? slAnchor - slAtrBuffer * atrVal : slAnchor + slAtrBuffer * atrVal)
slGeometryOk = candIsValidDir and (candIsLong ? slRaw < candEntry : slRaw > candEntry)
candSl = slGeometryOk ? slRaw : na
candRisk = slGeometryOk ? math.abs(candEntry - candSl) : na

candTp1 = slGeometryOk ? (candIsLong ? candEntry + tp1RMultiple * candRisk : candEntry - tp1RMultiple * candRisk) : na
tp2Objective = slGeometryOk ? (candIsLong ? f_nearestAbove(activeHighLevels, candEntry) : f_nearestBelow(activeLowLevels, candEntry)) : na
tp2Default = slGeometryOk ? (candIsLong ? candEntry + tp2RMultipleDefault * candRisk : candEntry - tp2RMultipleDefault * candRisk) : na
tp2Cap = slGeometryOk ? (candIsLong ? candEntry + tp2RMultipleCap * candRisk : candEntry - tp2RMultipleCap * candRisk) : na
tp2Raw = na(tp2Objective) ? tp2Default : tp2Objective
// A structural objective on the WRONG side of the default (i.e. offering
// LESS than 1R) is not a usable target — fall back to the default rather
// than publish a sub-1R objective.
tp2RawUsable = na(tp2Raw) ? na : (candIsLong ? (tp2Raw > candEntry ? tp2Raw : tp2Default) : (tp2Raw < candEntry ? tp2Raw : tp2Default))
candTp2 = slGeometryOk ? (candIsLong ? math.min(tp2RawUsable, tp2Cap) : math.max(tp2RawUsable, tp2Cap)) : na
candRr = slGeometryOk and not na(candTp2) ? math.abs(candTp2 - candEntry) / candRisk : na

// ── §21 Quality score 0-100 — independent, documented, non-overlapping
// components, each with an exact maximum, summing to exactly 100 at best
// case. NOT a probability/confidence/win-rate claim of any kind — a
// transparent, deterministic setup-quality score only.
//   component        max   rule
//   structure        15    confirmed swing type: HH/LL=15, LH/HL=10, EQH/EQL=5
//   trigger          15    fresh BOS=15, fresh CHoCH=12, MR/SR sweep-class=10
//   entry location   15    linear falloff to 0 as extension approaches the
//                          overextension ATR multiple (never negative)
//   momentum         10    ADX scaled linearly to the trend threshold, capped
//   volatility       10    full marks inside a "normal" 0.7-1.3 ATR-ratio
//                          band, linear falloff outside it
//   MTF alignment    15    HTF bias matches direction=15, flat=7.5, opposes=0
//   session          10    LONDON/NEW_YORK=10, ASIA=6, OTHER=2
//   RR quality       10    0 at minRR, scales up to +100% over minRR, capped
//
// P3 review §6 double-counting audit — two pairs deliberately share an
// input measurement but score a DIFFERENT property, not the same evidence
// twice:
//   qStructure vs qTrigger — qStructure scores the SWING PATTERN itself
//     (is the sequence of confirmed highs/lows genuinely trending: HH/LL
//     vs LH/HL vs EQH/EQL), independent of any single event. qTrigger
//     scores the TYPE OF THE SPECIFIC BREAK that fired THIS bar (a fresh
//     continuation BOS vs a character-changing CHoCH vs a liquidity-class
//     MR/SR event) relative to the already-established structureDirection.
//     A strong swing pattern (high qStructure) can pair with any trigger
//     type, and a BOS (high qTrigger) can occur against a weak or EQH/EQL
//     swing pattern — they are independent axes, not a restatement of one
//     fact under two names.
//   qEntryLocation vs candOverextended — both read the same underlying
//     ATR-normalized distance-from-anchor measurement, but for DIFFERENT
//     purposes: candOverextended is a binary HARD GATE (reject outright
//     beyond the threshold); qEntryLocation is a CONTINUOUS score that
//     rewards a closer entry among otherwise-ACCEPTABLE (not overextended)
//     candidates. Reusing one measurement as both an elimination gate and a
//     graduated ranking signal is a standard, non-duplicative pattern — it
//     is never counted as two separate pieces of independent evidence.
qStructure = candModel == "NA" ? 0.0 : (candIsLong ? (lastSwingHighType == "HH" ? 15.0 : lastSwingHighType == "LH" ? 10.0 : 5.0) : (lastSwingLowType == "LL" ? 15.0 : lastSwingLowType == "HL" ? 10.0 : 5.0))
qTrigger = lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and (lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_BOS" or lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_BOS") ? 15.0 :
     lastStructureEventBar == bar_index and (lastStructureEvent == "BULLISH_CHOCH" or lastStructureEvent == "BEARISH_CHOCH") ? 12.0 :
     candModel == "MR" or candModel == "SR" ? 10.0 : 0.0
qEntryLocation = candTriggered and not na(candAnchor) and atrVal > 0 ? math.max(0.0, 15.0 - 15.0 * (math.abs(candEntry - candAnchor) / (overextendAtrMult * atrVal))) : 0.0
qMomentum = adxTrendThreshold > 0 ? math.min(10.0, 10.0 * (adxVal / adxTrendThreshold)) : 0.0
qVolatility = atrRatio >= 0.7 and atrRatio <= 1.3 ? 10.0 : math.max(0.0, 10.0 - 10.0 * math.abs(atrRatio - 1.0))
qMtf = candModel == "NA" ? 0.0 : (candIsLong ? (htfBias == "BULL" ? 15.0 : htfBias == "FLAT" ? 7.5 : 0.0) : (htfBias == "BEAR" ? 15.0 : htfBias == "FLAT" ? 7.5 : 0.0))
qSession = session == "LONDON" or session == "NEW_YORK" ? 10.0 : session == "ASIA" ? 6.0 : 2.0
qRr = not na(candRr) and minRR > 0 ? math.min(10.0, math.max(0.0, 10.0 * (candRr - minRR) / minRR)) : 0.0
candQualityRaw = qStructure + qTrigger + qEntryLocation + qMomentum + qVolatility + qMtf + qSession + qRr
candQuality = math.min(100.0, math.max(0.0, candQualityRaw))   // defensive clamp — components sum to exactly 100 at best case (15+15+15+10+10+15+10+10)

// ── §27 WAIT-reason precedence (single authoritative reason, documented) ──
//  1. NEWS_SUPPRESSION   6. NO_TRIGGER
//  2. CHOP / TRANSITION  7. CONFIRMATION_INCOMPLETE
//  3. CORRECTION_ACTIVE  8. ENTRY_LATE
//  4. NO_ELIGIBLE_STRATEGY  9. OVEREXTENDED
//  5. NO_SETUP           10. NO_GOOD_ENTRY (quality)   11. RR_NOT_ACCEPTABLE
// NO_SETUP/NO_TRIGGER/RR_NOT_ACCEPTABLE now genuinely used for the first
// time in P3 — P1/P2 never had setups/triggers/RR to report on.
tradeReady = candTriggered and candLocationOk and slGeometryOk and not na(candRr)
qualityOk = tradeReady and candQuality >= qualityThreshold
rrOk = tradeReady and qualityOk and candRr >= minRR

waitReason = newsSuppressed ? "NEWS_SUPPRESSION" :
     officialRegime == "CHOP_UNCERTAIN" ? "CHOP" :
     officialRegime == "TRANSITION" ? "TRANSITION" :
     correctionActive ? "CORRECTION_ACTIVE" :
     not anyEligible ? "NO_ELIGIBLE_STRATEGY" :
     not anySetupReady ? "NO_SETUP" :
     not candTriggered ? "NO_TRIGGER" :
     not confirmedBar ? "CONFIRMATION_INCOMPLETE" :
     candEntryLate ? "ENTRY_LATE" :
     candOverextended ? "OVEREXTENDED" :
     not qualityOk ? "NO_GOOD_ENTRY" :
     not rrOk ? "RR_NOT_ACCEPTABLE" :
     "UNKNOWN"   // unreachable in practice — every gate above is exhaustive; UNKNOWN is the safe enum fallback if it were ever hit

// =============================================================================
// P5 — SIGNAL RECORDER + OUTCOME ENGINE (scaffolding, declared before use)
// =============================================================================
// P5 is NOT a second trading strategy. It consumes the EXACT existing P3
// approval event (the `if newSignalId != signalId` block below, itself
// gated by the unchanged `finalTradeApproved` conjunction) — no new signal
// detector exists anywhere in this file. See docs/PINE_P5.md for the full
// architecture, chronology rules, and eviction policy.
//
// Signal-bar chronology (critical, non-repaint rule): ENTRY = close of the
// confirmed signal bar (`candEntry = close`, unchanged from P3). That
// bar's OWN high/low could reflect price action that happened before its
// own close existed — using them to test SL/target would grant the system
// information from before the entry was actually filled. Outcome
// resolution therefore begins STRICTLY on the first bar AFTER the signal
// bar (`bar_index > rec.signalBarIndex`), never the signal bar itself.
//
// Same-bar ambiguity (mandatory conservative rule): a single OHLC bar does
// not reveal intrabar path. If a future bar's high/low would touch BOTH
// the initial SL and the success target, this is treated as FAIL — never
// inferred from candle color or an assumed open→high→low→close path.
// ── P5 review/fix: OPEN-record eviction correctness ───────────────────────
// A genuine OPEN signal must remain outcome-trackable until it terminates
// PASS or FAIL, no matter how many newer signals arrive. Storage is
// therefore split into three explicitly distinct concepts:
//   1. ACTIVE OPEN OUTCOME STATE (`openSignals`) — holds every currently
//      unresolved signal. NEVER capacity-evicted while OPEN. Only removed
//      the instant it resolves (moved into recentHistory below).
//   2. BOUNDED RECENT TERMINAL/DISPLAY HISTORY (`recentHistory`) — holds
//      only already-resolved (PASS/FAIL) records, FIFO-evicted oldest-
//      first once at capacity. Eviction here is always safe: the record's
//      one-time contribution to the lifetime aggregates below already
//      happened at the moment it resolved, and never depends on it still
//      being present in this array afterward.
//   3. LIFETIME AGGREGATES (p5Total*/p5Cumulative*/modelStats/etc.) —
//      plain `var` scalars/CategoryStat objects incremented exactly once
//      at creation time (totals) or exactly once at resolution time
//      (pass/fail/R/streaks), never derived by re-scanning either array.
// This guarantees total == PASS + FAIL + OPEN always, regardless of how
// long any individual signal stays open or how much display-history
// eviction has occurred in the meantime.
p5MaxTrackedSignals = input.int(300, "P5: Max Recent CLOSED-History Records (FIFO eviction, oldest-first — never evicts an OPEN signal)", minval = 10, group = "P5 Statistics")
// Pine resource safety valve: openSignals is intentionally UNBOUNDED in the
// sense that it is never capacity-evicted while a signal is open — but an
// unbounded array is still a theoretical resource concern if something
// pathological produced an unbounded number of simultaneously-open
// signals (never observed in practice: the frozen P3 gates make
// concurrent opens rare). p5MaxOpenSignals is a generous, essentially
// unreachable-in-practice ceiling that, if ever hit, does NOT evict an
// unresolved signal and does NOT silently pretend statistics are still
// complete — it latches `p5OpenCeilingBreached` and counts the untracked
// signal separately in `p5UntrackedSignals`, both exposed in the stats
// table, so the condition is visible rather than hidden.
p5MaxOpenSignals     = input.int(500, "P5: Max Concurrently-Tracked OPEN Signals (safety ceiling — never evicts an open signal; see docs/PINE_P5.md)", minval = 50, group = "P5 Statistics")
p5ShowStatsTable     = input.bool(true, "P5: Show Statistics Table", group = "P5 Statistics")
p5ShowRecentSignals  = input.bool(false, "P5: Show Recent Signals Table", group = "P5 Statistics")
p5RecentSignalsCount = input.int(10, "P5: Recent Signals Row Count", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = "P5 Statistics")

// Fixed, frozen vocabularies — P5 does not invent classifications. These
// mirror the exact existing model/regime/session strings this file already
// emits elsewhere (see §4 eligibility matrix and the `session` assignment).
var array<string> P5_MODELS      = array.from("TC", "PB", "BO", "MR", "SR")
var array<string> P5_REGIMES     = array.from("BULL_TREND", "BEAR_TREND", "RANGE", "COMPRESSION", "TRANSITION", "CHOP_UNCERTAIN", "HIGH_VOLATILITY")
var array<string> P5_SESSIONS    = array.from("ASIA", "LONDON", "NEW_YORK", "OTHER")
var array<string> P5_TIMEFRAMES  = array.from("5", "15", "30", "OTHER")

type CategoryStat
    string name
    int    total
    int    pass
    int    fail
    float  cumR

f_p5NewCategoryStats(names) =>
    arr = array.new<CategoryStat>()
    if array.size(names) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(names) - 1
            array.push(arr, CategoryStat.new(array.get(names, i), 0, 0, 0, 0.0))
    arr

var array<CategoryStat> modelStats     = f_p5NewCategoryStats(P5_MODELS)
var array<CategoryStat> regimeStats    = f_p5NewCategoryStats(P5_REGIMES)
var array<CategoryStat> sessionStats   = f_p5NewCategoryStats(P5_SESSIONS)
var array<CategoryStat> timeframeStats = f_p5NewCategoryStats(P5_TIMEFRAMES)

f_p5FindStat(arr, name) =>
    CategoryStat result = na
    if array.size(arr) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(arr) - 1
            cs = array.get(arr, i)
            if cs.name == name
                result := cs
    result

f_p5BumpTotal(arr, name) =>
    cs = f_p5FindStat(arr, name)
    if not na(cs)
        cs.total += 1

f_p5BumpResult(arr, name, isPass, rResult) =>
    cs = f_p5FindStat(arr, name)
    if not na(cs)
        if isPass
            cs.pass += 1
        else
            cs.fail += 1
        cs.cumR += rResult

f_p5TfBucket(tf) => (tf == "5" or tf == "15" or tf == "30") ? tf : "OTHER"

type SignalRecord
    string id
    string side                     // "BULLISH" / "BEARISH"
    int    signalBarTime
    int    signalBarIndex
    float  entry
    float  initialSl
    float  tp1
    float  tp2
    float  exitTarget                // always na in this indicator version — P3 does not populate EXIT_TARGET yet (see contract table row 25)
    float  successTarget             // the authoritative terminal PASS target: tp2 if present, else exitTarget (either/or, never both required)
    float  reportedRr
    string model
    string regime
    float  quality
    string timeframe
    string session
    string correctionStateAtEntry
    bool   barConfirmedAtEntry
    string status                    // "OPEN" / "PASS" / "FAIL" — exactly one, never a 4th state
    int    outcomeBarTime
    int    outcomeBarIndex
    float  outcomePrice
    float  rResult
    bool   sameBarAmbiguity

// `openSignals` — every currently-unresolved signal. Pushed to on
// creation; NEVER capacity-evicted. Removed only at the exact moment it
// resolves (see P5 OUTCOME RESOLUTION below), at which point it moves into
// `recentHistory`.
var array<SignalRecord> openSignals    = array.new<SignalRecord>()
// `recentHistory` — bounded, closed-only (PASS/FAIL) display/audit trail.
// Deterministic oldest-first FIFO eviction once at capacity (identical
// idiom to P2's activeHighLevels/activeLowLevels pattern) — always safe,
// since every record here already made its one-time lifetime-aggregate
// contribution at the moment it resolved, before ever being pushed here.
var array<SignalRecord> recentHistory  = array.new<SignalRecord>()

// ── Lifetime aggregates — survive array eviction by construction ─────────
var int    p5TotalSignals    = 0
var int    p5TotalPass       = 0
var int    p5TotalFail       = 0
var int    p5BuyTotal        = 0
var int    p5SellTotal       = 0
var int    p5BuyPass         = 0
var int    p5BuyFail         = 0
var int    p5SellPass        = 0
var int    p5SellFail        = 0
var float  p5CumulativeR     = 0.0
var float  p5BestR           = na
var float  p5WorstR          = na
var float  p5SumWinR         = 0.0
var int    p5WinCount        = 0
var float  p5SumLossR        = 0.0
var int    p5LossCount       = 0
var string p5CurrentStreakType = "NONE"
var int    p5CurrentStreakLen  = 0
var int    p5MaxPassStreak     = 0
var int    p5MaxFailStreak     = 0
var int    p5FirstSignalTime   = na
var int    p5LastSignalTime    = na
var bool   p5OpenCeilingBreached = false   // see p5MaxOpenSignals above — latched permanently if ever hit; never un-set
var int    p5UntrackedSignals    = 0       // count of signals that could not be tracked because the ceiling was already breached — exposed, never hidden

// NOTE: the P5 aggregate-update logic (formerly a helper function here) is
// inlined directly in the P5 OUTCOME RESOLUTION block below instead of
// being a called function — Pine Script does not permit a user-defined
// function to reassign global `var` scalars (only top-level script code
// can). f_p5BumpTotal/f_p5BumpResult above remain functions because they
// only mutate a UDT object's OWN field through a local reference (the
// object itself, not a global variable binding), which Pine does permit.

// ── §14 Correction hard blocker + §15 confirmation gate + all gates ───────
// combined into the single final boolean — every one of these must hold,
// with NO exception, for ANY trade to be considered.
var string lastEmittedOriginKey = "NA"
candOriginFresh = candOriginKey != "NA" and candOriginKey != lastEmittedOriginKey

finalTradeApproved = newsSuppressed == false and
     officialRegime != "CHOP_UNCERTAIN" and officialRegime != "TRANSITION" and
     not correctionActive and
     anyEligible and anySetupReady and candTriggered and
     confirmedBar and
     not candEntryLate and not candOverextended and
     qualityOk and rrOk and
     slGeometryOk and not na(candRr) and
     candOriginFresh

// ── §28/§29 Signal state machine — freeze-once, deterministic identity ───
// Freezing happens ONLY on the bar a trade is genuinely approved. Every
// frozen field is a `var` written exactly once per signal — later bars
// (including the very next one) never rewrite an already-frozen signal's
// historical values; a DIFFERENT later signal gets a brand-new identity
// instead of overwriting fields in place for audit purposes, but the
// contract only ever needs to report the MOST RECENT one, matching how
// every other "last event" field in this file already behaves.
var string signalId        = "NA"
var string signalSide      = "NA"       // "BULLISH" / "BEARISH" — the internal direction record; ACTION itself is computed fresh below, never derived backward from this
var float  signalEntry     = na
var float  signalSl        = na
var float  signalTp1       = na
var float  signalTp2       = na
var float  signalRr        = na
var string signalModel     = "NA"
var string signalRegime    = "NA"
var float  signalQuality   = na
var int    signalBarTime   = na
var string signalTimeframe = "NA"
var string signalSession   = "NA"

if confirmedBar and finalTradeApproved
    // Includes the ORIGIN bar (not just the trigger/current bar) so the ID
    // is self-documenting about which underlying setup opportunity produced
    // it, and remains unique even if the same model+direction fires again
    // later from a genuinely different origin.
    newSignalId = candModel + "_" + (candIsLong ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH") + "_O" + str.tostring(candSetupOriginBar) + "_T" + str.tostring(bar_index)
    if newSignalId != signalId   // defensive dedup — bar_index is unique per bar so this is always true in practice, but never re-freeze the identical id
        lastEmittedOriginKey := candOriginKey   // latch this origin so finalTradeApproved can never approve it again
        signalId := newSignalId
        signalSide := candIsLong ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH"
        signalEntry := candEntry
        signalSl := candSl
        signalTp1 := candTp1
        signalTp2 := candTp2
        signalRr := candRr
        signalModel := candModel
        signalRegime := officialRegime
        signalQuality := candQuality
        signalBarTime := time
        signalTimeframe := timeframe.period
        signalSession := session

        // ── P5 recorder hook — same event, same dedup, one record per
        // approval. Not a new signal detector: this is the identical
        // `newSignalId != signalId` condition the P3 freeze block already
        // uses. EXIT_TARGET is not yet populated by this indicator (always
        // na), so successTarget resolves to candTp2 under the current
        // engine — the either/or architecture is preserved for when/if a
        // future phase populates EXIT_TARGET.
        p5SuccessTarget = not na(candTp2) ? candTp2 : na
        // ── Pine resource safety valve (see p5MaxOpenSignals comment above).
        // If ever hit, the signal is NOT tracked (never evicting an existing
        // unresolved one instead), and the condition is latched/counted
        // rather than silently absorbed into a statistic that would then be
        // incomplete without saying so.
        if array.size(openSignals) >= p5MaxOpenSignals
            p5OpenCeilingBreached := true
            p5UntrackedSignals += 1
        else
            p5NewRecord = SignalRecord.new(id = newSignalId, side = candIsLong ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH", signalBarTime = time, signalBarIndex = bar_index, entry = candEntry, initialSl = candSl, tp1 = candTp1, tp2 = candTp2, exitTarget = na, successTarget = p5SuccessTarget, reportedRr = candRr, model = candModel, regime = officialRegime, quality = candQuality, timeframe = timeframe.period, session = session, correctionStateAtEntry = correctionStateStr, barConfirmedAtEntry = confirmedBar, status = "OPEN", outcomeBarTime = na, outcomeBarIndex = na, outcomePrice = na, rResult = na, sameBarAmbiguity = false)
            // NEVER capacity-evicted while open — see openSignals declaration.
            array.push(openSignals, p5NewRecord)
            p5TotalSignals += 1
            if na(p5FirstSignalTime)
                p5FirstSignalTime := time
            p5LastSignalTime := time
            if candIsLong
                p5BuyTotal += 1
            else
                p5SellTotal += 1
            f_p5BumpTotal(modelStats, candModel)
            f_p5BumpTotal(regimeStats, officialRegime)
            f_p5BumpTotal(sessionStats, session)
            f_p5BumpTotal(timeframeStats, f_p5TfBucket(timeframe.period))

// One-time consumption: a triggered-and-approved BO retest sequence (or a
// still-pending one that was merely evaluated) must not remain "active" to
// re-trigger on a later bar. TC/PB/MR/SR triggers are already inherently
// single-bar (gated on lastStructureEventBar/lastSweepBar == bar_index),
// so only BO's multi-bar pending state needs explicit consumption here.
if confirmedBar and boLongTrigger
    boLongActive := false
if confirmedBar and boShortTrigger
    boShortActive := false

// ── THE ACTION FIELD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The ONLY place in this entire file where "BUY"/"SELL" can be produced —
// gated behind `finalTradeApproved`, itself the conjunction of every gate
// above. If ANY gate is false, this always evaluates to "WAIT". There is no
// other assignment to contractAction anywhere else in the file.
contractAction = finalTradeApproved ? (candIsLong ? "BUY" : "SELL") : "WAIT"

// Published trade fields mirror the FROZEN signal on the bar it was
// approved, and stay NA on every other bar — never the live/current
// candidate values, which could differ bar-to-bar before/after approval.
outEntry      = finalTradeApproved ? signalEntry      : na
outSl         = finalTradeApproved ? signalSl         : na
outTp1        = finalTradeApproved ? signalTp1        : na
outTp2        = finalTradeApproved ? signalTp2        : na
outRr         = finalTradeApproved ? signalRr         : na
outModel      = finalTradeApproved ? signalModel      : "NA"
outSignalId   = finalTradeApproved ? signalId         : "NA"
outSignalTime = finalTradeApproved ? signalBarTime    : na
outQuality    = candTriggered ? candQuality : na   // quality is informative context even without a full approval — displayed whenever a trigger was at least evaluated
outSetupState = anySetupReady ? "SETUP_READY" : "NO_SETUP"
outTriggerState = candTriggered ? "TRIGGER_CONFIRMED" : (anySetupReady ? "TRIGGER_PENDING" : "NO_TRIGGER")
outConfirmationState = confirmedBar ? "CONFIRMED" : "PENDING"
outOverextensionState = candEntryLate ? "ENTRY_LATE" : candOverextended ? "OVEREXTENDED" : "NONE"
outRrValidationState = na(candRr) ? "NA" : (rrOk ? "ACCEPTABLE" : "RR_NOT_ACCEPTABLE")

// =============================================================================
// P5 — OUTCOME RESOLUTION (runs once per confirmed bar, over every OPEN
// tracked record). `bar_index > rec.signalBarIndex` (strict) guarantees a
// record created earlier THIS SAME bar is never evaluated against its own
// creation bar's high/low — see the chronology note in the scaffolding
// section above. Never repaints: OPEN can only ever become PASS or FAIL,
// exactly once, and a resolved record's fields are never written again.
// =============================================================================
// Iterated BACKWARD (high index to low) so array.remove() at the current
// index never disturbs not-yet-visited lower indices — the standard safe
// remove-during-iteration pattern. Guarded by array.size() > 0 exactly
// like every other loop in this file (see the P4B runtime-safety patch);
// `for i = array.size(openSignals) - 1 to 0` is itself safe here because
// the guard already ensures size >= 1, so `from = size-1 >= to = 0`
// always holds — a genuine descending range, not the empty-array
// auto-reverse pitfall the P4B patch fixed elsewhere.
if confirmedBar and array.size(openSignals) > 0
    for i = array.size(openSignals) - 1 to 0
        rec = array.get(openSignals, i)
        if bar_index > rec.signalBarIndex and not na(rec.successTarget)
            isLong = rec.side == "BULLISH"
            slHit     = isLong ? low  <= rec.initialSl     : high >= rec.initialSl
            targetHit = isLong ? high >= rec.successTarget : low  <= rec.successTarget
            resolved = slHit or targetHit
            // slHit-and-targetHit (same-bar ambiguity, mandatory conservative
            // FAIL) and slHit-only both resolve to FAIL; targetHit-only (and
            // only reachable when slHit is false) resolves to PASS. Never
            // both PASS and FAIL — exactly one terminal outcome.
            isPass = targetHit and not slHit
            if resolved
                risk = isLong ? rec.entry - rec.initialSl : rec.initialSl - rec.entry
                reward = isLong ? rec.successTarget - rec.entry : rec.entry - rec.successTarget
                rMultiple = isPass ? (risk > 0 ? reward / risk : na) : -1.0
                validR = na(rMultiple) ? 0.0 : rMultiple   // defensive only — risk<=0 is structurally unreachable (slGeometryOk gates finalTradeApproved before any signal can exist)
                rec.status := isPass ? "PASS" : "FAIL"
                rec.sameBarAmbiguity := slHit and targetHit
                rec.outcomeBarTime := time
                rec.outcomeBarIndex := bar_index
                rec.outcomePrice := isPass ? rec.successTarget : rec.initialSl
                rec.rResult := rMultiple
                // ── Inlined aggregate update (must be top-level script code,
                // not a called function — see the scaffolding note above on
                // why Pine forbids a function from reassigning global vars).
                // Runs EXACTLY ONCE per record, at the exact moment it
                // transitions OPEN -> PASS/FAIL — never again afterward,
                // since the record is removed from openSignals immediately
                // below and can never re-enter this loop.
                if isPass
                    p5TotalPass += 1
                    p5SumWinR += validR
                    p5WinCount += 1
                    if na(p5BestR) or validR > p5BestR
                        p5BestR := validR
                else
                    p5TotalFail += 1
                    p5SumLossR += validR
                    p5LossCount += 1
                    if na(p5WorstR) or validR < p5WorstR
                        p5WorstR := validR
                if isLong
                    if isPass
                        p5BuyPass += 1
                    else
                        p5BuyFail += 1
                else
                    if isPass
                        p5SellPass += 1
                    else
                        p5SellFail += 1
                p5CumulativeR += validR
                thisStreakType = isPass ? "PASS" : "FAIL"
                if p5CurrentStreakType == thisStreakType
                    p5CurrentStreakLen += 1
                else
                    p5CurrentStreakType := thisStreakType
                    p5CurrentStreakLen := 1
                if isPass and p5CurrentStreakLen > p5MaxPassStreak
                    p5MaxPassStreak := p5CurrentStreakLen
                if not isPass and p5CurrentStreakLen > p5MaxFailStreak
                    p5MaxFailStreak := p5CurrentStreakLen
                f_p5BumpResult(modelStats, rec.model, isPass, validR)
                f_p5BumpResult(regimeStats, rec.regime, isPass, validR)
                f_p5BumpResult(sessionStats, rec.session, isPass, validR)
                f_p5BumpResult(timeframeStats, f_p5TfBucket(rec.timeframe), isPass, validR)
                // Move from the never-evicted OPEN tracker into the bounded
                // closed-only display history. array.remove() at index i is
                // safe here specifically because the loop walks backward.
                array.remove(openSignals, i)
                if array.size(recentHistory) >= p5MaxTrackedSignals
                    array.shift(recentHistory)   // closed-only FIFO eviction — the evicted record already made its one-time aggregate contribution above
                array.push(recentHistory, rec)

// ── §35 Alert conditions — prepared, never auto-configured/sent ──────────
// alertcondition() only registers a condition an operator may manually wire
// up inside TradingView's own Alert dialog; it never creates an alert,
// sends a webhook, or executes anything by itself.
alertcondition(finalTradeApproved and candIsLong, title = "XAUUSD Adaptive Master — Confirmed BUY", message = "XAUUSD Adaptive Master: confirmed BUY signal ({{ticker}}, {{interval}})")
alertcondition(finalTradeApproved and not candIsLong, title = "XAUUSD Adaptive Master — Confirmed SELL", message = "XAUUSD Adaptive Master: confirmed SELL signal ({{ticker}}, {{interval}})")

// =============================================================================
// CONTRACT TABLE — Phase 2B CONTRACT_VERSION=1 (unchanged — this is an
// additive extension, not a breaking contract change). P1 fields unchanged;
// P2 adds 20 structure-owned fields. Every field this indicator does not yet
// own is emitted as literal "NA", matching the MCP parser's null-compatible
// representation. Nothing here is fabricated on Pine's behalf.
// =============================================================================
var table contractTable = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 50, border_width = 1, border_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.gray)

f_row(tbl, r, k, v) =>
    table.cell(tbl, 0, r, k, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, r, v, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.yellow, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 0), text_halign = text.align_left)

if barstate.islast
    f_row(contractTable, 0,  "CONTRACT_VERSION", str.tostring(CONTRACT_VERSION))
    f_row(contractTable, 1,  "INDICATOR_VERSION", INDICATOR_VERSION)
    f_row(contractTable, 2,  "SYMBOL", syminfo.tickerid)
    f_row(contractTable, 3,  "EXECUTION_TF", timeframe.period)
    f_row(contractTable, 4,  "CONTEXT_TF", htfTimeframe)
    f_row(contractTable, 5,  "BAR_TIME", str.tostring(time))
    f_row(contractTable, 6,  "BAR_INDEX", str.tostring(bar_index))
    f_row(contractTable, 7,  "BAR_CONFIRMED", confirmedBar ? "1" : "0")
    f_row(contractTable, 8,  "REGIME", officialRegime)
    f_row(contractTable, 9,  "CORRECTION_STATE", correctionStateStr)
    f_row(contractTable, 10, "CORRECTION_REASON", correctionActive ? correctionEvidence : "NA")
    f_row(contractTable, 11, "MODEL", finalTradeApproved ? outModel : "NA")
    f_row(contractTable, 12, "SETUP_STATE", outSetupState)
    f_row(contractTable, 13, "TRIGGER_STATE", outTriggerState)
    f_row(contractTable, 14, "CONFIRMATION_STATE", outConfirmationState)
    f_row(contractTable, 15, "QUALITY", na(outQuality) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outQuality, "#.#"))
    f_row(contractTable, 16, "QUALITY_THRESHOLD", str.tostring(qualityThreshold, "#.#"))
    f_row(contractTable, 17, "OVEREXTENSION_STATE", outOverextensionState)
    f_row(contractTable, 18, "RR_VALIDATION_STATE", outRrValidationState)
    f_row(contractTable, 19, "ACTION", contractAction)
    f_row(contractTable, 20, "WAIT_REASON", finalTradeApproved ? "NA" : waitReason)
    f_row(contractTable, 21, "ENTRY", na(outEntry) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outEntry))
    f_row(contractTable, 22, "SL", na(outSl) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outSl))
    f_row(contractTable, 23, "TP1", na(outTp1) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outTp1))
    f_row(contractTable, 24, "TP2", na(outTp2) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outTp2))
    f_row(contractTable, 25, "EXIT_TARGET", "NA")
    f_row(contractTable, 26, "RR", na(outRr) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outRr, "#.##"))
    f_row(contractTable, 27, "SESSION", session)
    f_row(contractTable, 28, "SIGNAL_ID", outSignalId)
    f_row(contractTable, 29, "SIGNAL_BAR_TIME", na(outSignalTime) ? "NA" : str.tostring(outSignalTime))
    // P2 additions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    f_row(contractTable, 30, "STRUCTURE_STATE", structureDirection)
    f_row(contractTable, 31, "LAST_STRUCTURE_EVENT", lastStructureEvent)
    f_row(contractTable, 32, "LAST_STRUCTURE_EVENT_BAR", na(lastStructureEventBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastStructureEventBar))
    f_row(contractTable, 33, "LAST_SWING_HIGH", na(lastSwingHigh) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingHigh))
    f_row(contractTable, 34, "LAST_SWING_HIGH_TYPE", lastSwingHighType)
    f_row(contractTable, 35, "LAST_SWING_LOW", na(lastSwingLow) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingLow))
    f_row(contractTable, 36, "LAST_SWING_LOW_TYPE", lastSwingLowType)
    f_row(contractTable, 37, "LAST_BOS_DIRECTION", lastBosDirection)
    f_row(contractTable, 38, "LAST_BOS_BAR", na(lastBosBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastBosBar))
    f_row(contractTable, 39, "LAST_CHOCH_DIRECTION", lastChochDirection)
    f_row(contractTable, 40, "LAST_CHOCH_BAR", na(lastChochBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastChochBar))
    f_row(contractTable, 41, "LAST_SWEEP_TYPE", lastSweepType)
    f_row(contractTable, 42, "LAST_SWEEP_BAR", na(lastSweepBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSweepBar))
    f_row(contractTable, 43, "PDH", na(pdh) ? "NA" : str.tostring(pdh))
    f_row(contractTable, 44, "PDL", na(pdl) ? "NA" : str.tostring(pdl))
    f_row(contractTable, 45, "LAST_DAILY_SWEEP", lastDailySweep)
    f_row(contractTable, 46, "DISPLACEMENT_STATE", displacementState)
    f_row(contractTable, 47, "RANGE_STATE", rangeState)
    f_row(contractTable, 48, "RANGE_HIGH", na(rangeHigh) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rangeHigh))
    f_row(contractTable, 49, "RANGE_LOW", na(rangeLow) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rangeLow))

// =============================================================================
// DEBUG TABLE — internal audit state, OFF by default (debugMode input).
// Extended in P2 with structure/pivot/range chronology detail not carried
// in the compact contract table.
// =============================================================================
var table debugTable = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 56, border_width = 1, border_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.gray)

// Most-recent-level convenience reads for the debug table — the active
// arrays themselves (not these) are what BOS/CHoCH/sweep detection uses.
activeHighCount = array.size(activeHighLevels)
activeLowCount  = array.size(activeLowLevels)
lastHighLevelConsumed = activeHighCount > 0 ? array.get(activeHighLevels, activeHighCount - 1).consumed : false
lastHighLevelSwept    = activeHighCount > 0 ? array.get(activeHighLevels, activeHighCount - 1).swept : false
lastLowLevelConsumed  = activeLowCount  > 0 ? array.get(activeLowLevels, activeLowCount - 1).consumed : false
lastLowLevelSwept     = activeLowCount  > 0 ? array.get(activeLowLevels, activeLowCount - 1).swept : false

if debugMode and barstate.islast
    f_row(debugTable, 0,  "regime_candidate", regimeCandidate)
    f_row(debugTable, 1,  "regime_streak", str.tostring(regimeStreak))
    f_row(debugTable, 2,  "official_regime", officialRegime)
    f_row(debugTable, 3,  "prior_official_regime", priorOfficialRegime)
    f_row(debugTable, 4,  "htf_bias", htfBias)
    f_row(debugTable, 5,  "correction_active", str.tostring(correctionActive))
    f_row(debugTable, 6,  "correction_side", correctionSide)
    f_row(debugTable, 7,  "corr_start_bar", na(corrStartBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(corrStartBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 8,  "corr_resolved_bar", na(corrResolvedBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(corrResolvedBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 9,  "corr_resolved_side", corrResolvedSide)
    f_row(debugTable, 10, "corr_recover_streak", str.tostring(corrRecoverStreak))
    f_row(debugTable, 11, "adx", str.tostring(adxVal, "#.##"))
    f_row(debugTable, 12, "atr_ratio", str.tostring(atrRatio, "#.##"))
    f_row(debugTable, 13, "bb_width_ratio", str.tostring(bbWidthRatio, "#.##"))
    f_row(debugTable, 14, "flip_count", str.tostring(flipCount))
    f_row(debugTable, 15, "wait_reason", waitReason)
    f_row(debugTable, 16, "swing_high_loc_bar", na(lastSwingHighBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingHighBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 17, "swing_high_confirm_bar", na(lastSwingHighConfirmBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingHighConfirmBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 18, "swing_high_born_close_consumed", str.tostring(lastSwingHighBornConsumed))
    f_row(debugTable, 19, "active_high_levels_count", str.tostring(activeHighCount))
    f_row(debugTable, 20, "last_high_level_consumed", str.tostring(lastHighLevelConsumed))
    f_row(debugTable, 21, "last_high_level_swept", str.tostring(lastHighLevelSwept))
    f_row(debugTable, 22, "swing_low_loc_bar", na(lastSwingLowBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingLowBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 23, "swing_low_confirm_bar", na(lastSwingLowConfirmBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(lastSwingLowConfirmBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 24, "swing_low_born_close_consumed", str.tostring(lastSwingLowBornConsumed))
    f_row(debugTable, 25, "active_low_levels_count", str.tostring(activeLowCount))
    f_row(debugTable, 26, "last_low_level_consumed", str.tostring(lastLowLevelConsumed))
    f_row(debugTable, 27, "last_low_level_swept", str.tostring(lastLowLevelSwept))
    f_row(debugTable, 28, "regime_vs_structure_agree", str.tostring(not isDirectionalTrend(officialRegime) or (officialRegime == "BULL_TREND" and structureDirection == "BULLISH") or (officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND" and structureDirection == "BEARISH")))
    f_row(debugTable, 29, "range_id", str.tostring(rangeId))
    f_row(debugTable, 30, "range_anchor_bar", na(rangeAnchorBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rangeAnchorBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 31, "range_confirm_bar", na(rangeConfirmBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rangeConfirmBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 32, "range_regime_streak", str.tostring(rangeRegimeStreak))
    f_row(debugTable, 33, "displacement_body_ratio", str.tostring(bodyRatio, "#.##"))
    f_row(debugTable, 34, "max_active_levels", str.tostring(maxActiveLevels))
    f_row(debugTable, 35, "pivot_right_bars", str.tostring(pivotRightBars))
    f_row(debugTable, 36, "candidate_model", candModel)
    f_row(debugTable, 37, "candidate_triggered", str.tostring(candTriggered))
    f_row(debugTable, 38, "candidate_quality", str.tostring(candQuality, "#.#"))
    f_row(debugTable, 39, "candidate_rr", na(candRr) ? "NA" : str.tostring(candRr, "#.##"))
    f_row(debugTable, 40, "candidate_overextended", str.tostring(candOverextended))
    f_row(debugTable, 41, "candidate_entry_late", str.tostring(candEntryLate))
    f_row(debugTable, 42, "quality_ok", str.tostring(qualityOk))
    f_row(debugTable, 43, "rr_ok", str.tostring(rrOk))
    f_row(debugTable, 44, "final_trade_approved", str.tostring(finalTradeApproved))
    f_row(debugTable, 45, "bo_long_active", str.tostring(boLongActive))
    f_row(debugTable, 46, "bo_short_active", str.tostring(boShortActive))
    f_row(debugTable, 47, "bo_long_retest_bar", na(boLongRetestBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(boLongRetestBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 48, "bo_short_retest_bar", na(boShortRetestBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(boShortRetestBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 49, "candidate_setup_origin_bar", na(candSetupOriginBar) ? "NA" : str.tostring(candSetupOriginBar))
    f_row(debugTable, 50, "candidate_max_late_bars", str.tostring(candMaxLateBars))
    f_row(debugTable, 51, "candidate_origin_key", candOriginKey)
    f_row(debugTable, 52, "last_emitted_origin_key", lastEmittedOriginKey)
    f_row(debugTable, 53, "candidate_origin_fresh", str.tostring(candOriginFresh))
    f_row(debugTable, 54, "mr_long_displacement_blocked", str.tostring(mrLongDisplacementBlocked))
    f_row(debugTable, 55, "mr_short_displacement_blocked", str.tostring(mrShortDisplacementBlocked))

// =============================================================================
// P5 — STATISTICS TABLE (position.bottom_left — never collides with the
// authoritative contractTable at top_right or debugTable at bottom_right).
// CRITICAL: this table carries NO "CONTRACT_VERSION" row, so it can never
// be mistaken for the authoritative machine-readable contract by the
// anchor-based MCP table selection (src/core/xauusd.js
// CONTRACT_TABLE_ANCHOR). It is purely informational/statistical.
// =============================================================================
f_p5FmtCat(cs) =>
    openN = cs.total - cs.pass - cs.fail
    closedN = cs.pass + cs.fail
    rateStr = closedN > 0 ? str.tostring(cs.pass / closedN * 100, "#.#") + "%" : "NA"
    str.tostring(cs.total) + " (P" + str.tostring(cs.pass) + "/F" + str.tostring(cs.fail) + "/O" + str.tostring(openN) + ") " + rateStr + " R=" + str.tostring(cs.cumR, "#.##")

var table p5StatsTable = table.new(position.bottom_left, 2, 49, border_width = 1, border_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.gray)

if p5ShowStatsTable and barstate.islast
    // All figures below are derived ONLY from lifetime scalars/CategoryStat
    // objects — never by re-scanning openSignals/recentHistory — so they
    // are correct regardless of recentHistory eviction and regardless of
    // how long any individual signal has been open.
    p5Closed = p5TotalPass + p5TotalFail
    p5Open = p5TotalSignals - p5TotalPass - p5TotalFail
    p5PassRate = p5Closed > 0 ? str.tostring(p5TotalPass / p5Closed * 100, "#.#") + "%" : "NA"
    p5AvgR = p5Closed > 0 ? str.tostring(p5CumulativeR / p5Closed, "#.##") : "NA"
    p5AvgWinR = p5WinCount > 0 ? str.tostring(p5SumWinR / p5WinCount, "#.##") : "NA"
    p5AvgLossR = p5LossCount > 0 ? str.tostring(p5SumLossR / p5LossCount, "#.##") : "NA"
    buyOpen = p5BuyTotal - p5BuyPass - p5BuyFail
    sellOpen = p5SellTotal - p5SellPass - p5SellFail
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 0,  "P5_TOTAL_SIGNALS", str.tostring(p5TotalSignals))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 1,  "P5_PASS", str.tostring(p5TotalPass))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 2,  "P5_FAIL", str.tostring(p5TotalFail))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 3,  "P5_OPEN", str.tostring(p5Open))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 4,  "P5_CLOSED", str.tostring(p5Closed))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 5,  "P5_PASS_RATE", p5PassRate)
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 6,  "P5_BUY_TOTAL", str.tostring(p5BuyTotal))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 7,  "P5_BUY_PASS", str.tostring(p5BuyPass))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 8,  "P5_BUY_FAIL", str.tostring(p5BuyFail))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 9,  "P5_BUY_OPEN", str.tostring(buyOpen))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 10, "P5_SELL_TOTAL", str.tostring(p5SellTotal))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 11, "P5_SELL_PASS", str.tostring(p5SellPass))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 12, "P5_SELL_FAIL", str.tostring(p5SellFail))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 13, "P5_SELL_OPEN", str.tostring(sellOpen))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 14, "P5_CUMULATIVE_R", str.tostring(p5CumulativeR, "#.##"))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 15, "P5_AVG_R_PER_CLOSED", p5AvgR)
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 16, "P5_AVG_WIN_R", p5AvgWinR)
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 17, "P5_AVG_LOSS_R", p5AvgLossR)
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 18, "P5_BEST_R", na(p5BestR) ? "NA" : str.tostring(p5BestR, "#.##"))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 19, "P5_WORST_R", na(p5WorstR) ? "NA" : str.tostring(p5WorstR, "#.##"))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 20, "P5_CURRENT_STREAK", p5CurrentStreakType + " x" + str.tostring(p5CurrentStreakLen))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 21, "P5_MAX_PASS_STREAK", str.tostring(p5MaxPassStreak))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 22, "P5_MAX_FAIL_STREAK", str.tostring(p5MaxFailStreak))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 23, "P5_FIRST_SIGNAL_TIME", na(p5FirstSignalTime) ? "NA" : str.tostring(p5FirstSignalTime))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 24, "P5_LAST_SIGNAL_TIME", na(p5LastSignalTime) ? "NA" : str.tostring(p5LastSignalTime))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 25, "P5_OPEN_TRACKED_COUNT", str.tostring(array.size(openSignals)))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 26, "P5_RECENT_HISTORY_COUNT", str.tostring(array.size(recentHistory)))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 27, "P5_OPEN_CEILING_BREACHED", str.tostring(p5OpenCeilingBreached))
    f_row(p5StatsTable, 28, "P5_UNTRACKED_SIGNALS", str.tostring(p5UntrackedSignals))
    if array.size(P5_MODELS) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(P5_MODELS) - 1
            f_row(p5StatsTable, 29 + i, "P5_MODEL_" + array.get(P5_MODELS, i), f_p5FmtCat(f_p5FindStat(modelStats, array.get(P5_MODELS, i))))
    if array.size(P5_REGIMES) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(P5_REGIMES) - 1
            f_row(p5StatsTable, 34 + i, "P5_REGIME_" + array.get(P5_REGIMES, i), f_p5FmtCat(f_p5FindStat(regimeStats, array.get(P5_REGIMES, i))))
    if array.size(P5_SESSIONS) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(P5_SESSIONS) - 1
            f_row(p5StatsTable, 41 + i, "P5_SESSION_" + array.get(P5_SESSIONS, i), f_p5FmtCat(f_p5FindStat(sessionStats, array.get(P5_SESSIONS, i))))
    if array.size(P5_TIMEFRAMES) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(P5_TIMEFRAMES) - 1
            f_row(p5StatsTable, 45 + i, "P5_TF_" + array.get(P5_TIMEFRAMES, i), f_p5FmtCat(f_p5FindStat(timeframeStats, array.get(P5_TIMEFRAMES, i))))

// ── P5 — RECENT SIGNALS TABLE (bounded, most-recent-first, optional) ──────
var table p5RecentTable = table.new(position.middle_left, 8, 31, border_width = 1, border_color = color.gray, frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.gray)

if p5ShowRecentSignals and barstate.islast
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 0, 0, "ID", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 1, 0, "SIDE", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 2, 0, "MODEL", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 3, 0, "ENTRY", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 4, 0, "SL", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 5, 0, "TARGET", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 6, 0, "STATUS", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    table.cell(p5RecentTable, 7, 0, "R", text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.blue, 0))
    // Show ALL currently-open signals first (normally very few, given how
    // selective the frozen gates are), then fill any remaining row budget
    // with the most recent CLOSED records. This never depends on a single
    // merged array, matching the openSignals/recentHistory split above.
    openCount = array.size(openSignals)
    rowN = 0
    if openCount > 0
        for o = 0 to math.min(openCount, p5RecentSignalsCount) - 1
            rec2 = array.get(openSignals, o)
            rowN += 1
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 0, rowN, rec2.id, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 1, rowN, rec2.side, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 2, rowN, rec2.model, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 3, rowN, str.tostring(rec2.entry), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 4, rowN, str.tostring(rec2.initialSl), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 5, rowN, na(rec2.successTarget) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rec2.successTarget), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 6, rowN, rec2.status, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 7, rowN, na(rec2.rResult) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rec2.rResult, "#.##"), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
    remainingBudget = p5RecentSignalsCount - rowN
    historyTotal = array.size(recentHistory)
    if remainingBudget > 0 and historyTotal > 0
        for h = 0 to math.min(historyTotal, remainingBudget) - 1
            rec3 = array.get(recentHistory, historyTotal - 1 - h)   // most recent closed first
            rowN += 1
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 0, rowN, rec3.id, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 1, rowN, rec3.side, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 2, rowN, rec3.model, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 3, rowN, str.tostring(rec3.entry), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 4, rowN, str.tostring(rec3.initialSl), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 5, rowN, na(rec3.successTarget) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rec3.successTarget), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 6, rowN, rec3.status, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
            table.cell(p5RecentTable, 7, rowN, na(rec3.rResult) ? "NA" : str.tostring(rec3.rResult, "#.##"), text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)

// ── Minimal default visuals ────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(emaFast, "EMA Fast", color = color.new(color.aqua, 0), linewidth = 1)
plot(emaSlow, "EMA Slow", color = color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth = 1)

// Signal markers — ONLY for an actually-approved signal, on the bar it was
// approved (never a repainted/backdated marker; `finalTradeApproved` is
// itself confirmed-bar gated so this can never mark an unconfirmed bar).
plotshape(finalTradeApproved and candIsLong, title = "BUY Signal", style = shape.triangleup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(color.green, 0), size = size.small)
plotshape(finalTradeApproved and not candIsLong, title = "SELL Signal", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.red, 0), size = size.small)

// Correction (a sub-state of a directional trend, not a regime value itself)
// overrides the base regime tint so it's visually distinct in debug mode.
regimeTintColor = correctionActive ? color.new(color.purple, 92) :
     officialRegime == "BULL_TREND" ? color.new(color.green, 92) :
     officialRegime == "BEAR_TREND" ? color.new(color.red, 92) :
     officialRegime == "COMPRESSION" ? color.new(color.blue, 92) :
     officialRegime == "HIGH_VOLATILITY" ? color.new(color.fuchsia, 92) :
     officialRegime == "TRANSITION" ? color.new(color.yellow, 92) :
     na
bgcolor(debugMode ? regimeTintColor : na, title = "Regime Tint (debug only)")

// Bounded recent-event structure visuals — debug only, last swing levels
// only (never hundreds of historical labels).
plot(debugMode and not na(lastSwingHigh) ? lastSwingHigh : na, "Last Swing High", color = color.new(color.red, 40), style = plot.style_circles)
plot(debugMode and not na(lastSwingLow) ? lastSwingLow : na, "Last Swing Low", color = color.new(color.green, 40), style = plot.style_circles)
plot(debugMode and rangeState == "ACTIVE" and not na(rangeHigh) ? rangeHigh : na, "Anchored Range High", color = color.new(color.blue, 30), style = plot.style_linebr)
plot(debugMode and rangeState == "ACTIVE" and not na(rangeLow) ? rangeLow : na, "Anchored Range Low", color = color.new(color.blue, 30), style = plot.style_linebr)

// =============================================================================
// STRATEGY EXECUTION (strategy counterpart ONLY — this section does not
// exist in the indicator file; everything above this point is byte-for-
// byte identical to pine/XAUUSD_Adaptive_Master.pine, enforced by
// tests/pine_p5_strategy_parity.test.js).
//
// Places real strategy.entry()/strategy.exit() orders using the IDENTICAL
// finalTradeApproved/candIsLong/signalSl/signalTp2 values the indicator
// already computes and freezes above — never a second, independently-
// derived trading algorithm. No hidden Strategy-Tester-only entry filter
// and no hidden favorable-exit logic exists anywhere in this block.
//
// DOCUMENTED EXECUTION-MODEL DIFFERENCE FROM THE P5 CUSTOM RECORDER (see
// docs/PINE_P5.md "Strategy Tester vs custom recorder" for full detail):
// pyramiding=0 means TradingView's Strategy Tester broker emulator can
// hold at most ONE open position at a time, whereas the indicator's P5
// openSignals array can legitimately track MULTIPLE simultaneous OPEN
// signals if the frozen engine produces them (see §12 of the P5 spec).
// This is a genuine, disclosed difference in the two systems' execution
// models — it is never hidden. The P5 recorder inside the indicator
// remains the authoritative, deterministic PASS/FAIL source of truth,
// exactly as documented; Strategy Tester here is an additional technical
// cross-check on entry/SL/TP parity only, never a second source of truth
// for win-rate statistics, and its P&L must never be interpreted as proof
// of future performance.
// =============================================================================
if confirmedBar and finalTradeApproved
    if candIsLong
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long)
    else
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short)

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("Exit Long", "Long", stop = signalSl, limit = signalTp2)
if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("Exit Short", "Short", stop = signalSl, limit = signalTp2)
